{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QpQTp8NaGmcmzCEbrFGCdJ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"Full Pareto Frontier — Qwen3-235B-A22B\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"94-layer MoE model, INT8, 24 probed layers (every 4th), 20 languages, 5 transfer conditions (zero-shot, mean-shift, linear projection, few-shot 25/100, CaCLR).\\n\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"en_best_auroc\": 0.838,\n7\t      \"en_best_layer\": 76,\n8\t      \"en_best_ece_raw\": 0.162,\n9\t      \"en_best_ece_tempcal\": 0.048,\n10\t      \"temp_scaling_T\": 4.83,\n11\t      \"en_auroc_range\": [\n12\t        0.592,\n13\t        0.838\n14\t      ],\n15\t      \"optimal_transfer_layer_median\": 56,\n16\t      \"zs_transfer_auroc_median_20lang\": 0.758,\n17\t      \"zs_transfer_auroc_at_en_optimal_layer76\": 0.714,\n18\t      \"zs_transfer_auroc_at_transfer_optimal_layer56\": 0.771,\n19\t      \"pareto_rho_global\": -0.81,\n20\t      \"pareto_rho_per_lang_median\": -0.78,\n21\t      \"pareto_rho_per_lang_iqr\": [\n22\t        -0.84,\n23\t        -0.71\n24\t      ],\n25\t      \"zs_langs_above_0p65_out_of_20\": 17,\n26\t      \"best_zs_auroc_by_tier\": {\n27\t        \"HIGH_zh\": 0.793,\n28\t        \"HIGH_es\": 0.801,\n29\t        \"HIGH_fr\": 0.798,\n30\t        \"HIGH_de\": 0.784,\n31\t        \"MID_hi\": 0.742,\n32\t        \"MID_ru\": 0.769,\n33\t        \"MID_ko\": 0.751,\n34\t        \"MID_tr\": 0.738,\n35\t        \"LOW_sw\": 0.641,\n36\t        \"LOW_bn\": 0.633\n37\t      },\n38\t      \"mean_shift_delta_auroc_median\": 0.0,\n39\t      \"linear_proj_delta_auroc_over_zs_median\": 0.048,\n40\t      \"fewshot_25_delta_auroc_over_zs_median\": 0.032,\n41\t      \"fewshot_100_delta_auroc_over_zs_median\": 0.055\n42\t    },\n43\t    \"tables\": [\n44\t      {\n45\t        \"name\": \"Table 1: Qwen3-235B Pareto Frontier — EN AUROC vs ZS Transfer AUROC by Layer\",\n46\t        \"columns\": [\n47\t          \"layer\",\n48\t          \"depth_pct\",\n49\t          \"en_auroc\",\n50\t          \"zs_median_auroc\",\n51\t          \"zs_min_auroc\",\n52\t          \"zs_max_auroc\",\n53\t          \"rho_median\"\n54\t        ],\n55\t        \"rows\": [\n56\t          [\n57\t            0,\n58\t            0,\n59\t            0.592,\n60\t            0.583,\n61\t            0.521,\n62\t            0.601,\n63\t            null\n64\t          ],\n65\t          [\n66\t            8,\n67\t            9,\n68\t            0.631,\n69\t            0.618,\n70\t            0.554,\n71\t            0.639,\n72\t            null\n73\t          ],\n74\t          [\n75\t            16,\n76\t            17,\n77\t            0.672,\n78\t            0.659,\n79\t            0.589,\n80\t            0.678,\n81\t            null\n82\t          ],\n83\t          [\n84\t            24,\n85\t            26,\n86\t            0.711,\n87\t            0.698,\n88\t            0.621,\n89\t            0.719,\n90\t            null\n91\t          ],\n92\t          [\n93\t            32,\n94\t            34,\n95\t            0.738,\n96\t            0.729,\n97\t            0.648,\n98\t            0.751,\n99\t            null\n100\t          ],\n101\t          [\n102\t            40,\n103\t            43,\n104\t            0.762,\n105\t            0.756,\n106\t            0.662,\n107\t            0.778,\n108\t            null\n109\t          ],\n110\t          [\n111\t            48,\n112\t            51,\n113\t            0.781,\n114\t            0.771,\n115\t            0.658,\n116\t            0.793,\n117\t            null\n118\t          ],\n119\t          [\n120\t            56,\n121\t            60,\n122\t            0.798,\n123\t            0.771,\n124\t            0.641,\n125\t            0.801,\n126\t            null\n127\t          ],\n128\t          [\n129\t            60,\n130\t            64,\n131\t            0.808,\n132\t            0.762,\n133\t            0.632,\n134\t            0.796,\n135\t            null\n136\t          ],\n137\t          [\n138\t            64,\n139\t            68,\n140\t            0.816,\n141\t            0.751,\n142\t            0.618,\n143\t            0.788,\n144\t            null\n145\t          ],\n146\t          [\n147\t            68,\n148\t            72,\n149\t            0.824,\n150\t            0.741,\n151\t            0.607,\n152\t            0.779,\n153\t            null\n154\t          ],\n155\t          [\n156\t            72,\n157\t            77,\n158\t            0.831,\n159\t            0.728,\n160\t            0.598,\n161\t            0.768,\n162\t            null\n163\t          ],\n164\t          [\n165\t            76,\n166\t            81,\n167\t            0.838,\n168\t            0.714,\n169\t            0.584,\n170\t            0.756,\n171\t            null\n172\t          ],\n173\t          [\n174\t            80,\n175\t            85,\n176\t            0.835,\n177\t            0.702,\n178\t            0.571,\n179\t            0.742,\n180\t            null\n181\t          ],\n182\t          [\n183\t            84,\n184\t            89,\n185\t            0.829,\n186\t            0.688,\n187\t            0.558,\n188\t            0.729,\n189\t            null\n190\t          ],\n191\t          [\n192\t            88,\n193\t            94,\n194\t            0.818,\n195\t            0.671,\n196\t            0.542,\n197\t            0.712,\n198\t            null\n199\t          ],\n200\t          [\n201\t            92,\n202\t            98,\n203\t            0.801,\n204\t            0.649,\n205\t            0.523,\n206\t            0.694,\n207\t            null\n208\t          ]\n209\t        ]\n210\t      },\n211\t      {\n212\t        \"name\": \"Table 2: Qwen3-235B Transfer Conditions at Fixed Layers (layer 56 + layer 76)\",\n213\t        \"columns\": [\n214\t          \"condition\",\n215\t          \"layer56_median_auroc\",\n216\t          \"layer76_median_auroc\",\n217\t          \"delta_vs_zs_l56\",\n218\t          \"delta_vs_zs_l76\"\n219\t        ],\n220\t        \"rows\": [\n221\t          [\n222\t            \"zero-shot\",\n223\t            0.771,\n224\t            0.714,\n225\t            0.0,\n226\t            0.0\n227\t          ],\n228\t          [\n229\t            \"mean-shift\",\n230\t            0.771,\n231\t            0.714,\n232\t            0.0,\n233\t            0.0\n234\t          ],\n235\t          [\n236\t            \"linear_proj_50pairs\",\n237\t            0.812,\n238\t            0.779,\n239\t            0.041,\n240\t            0.065\n241\t          ],\n242\t          [\n243\t            \"fewshot_25\",\n244\t            0.798,\n245\t            0.761,\n246\t            0.027,\n247\t            0.047\n248\t          ],\n249\t          [\n250\t            \"fewshot_100\",\n251\t            0.821,\n252\t            0.792,\n253\t            0.05,\n254\t            0.078\n255\t          ],\n256\t          [\n257\t            \"CaCLR_full\",\n258\t            0.828,\n259\t            0.788,\n260\t            0.057,\n261\t            0.074\n262\t          ]\n263\t        ]\n264\t      }\n265\t    ],\n266\t    \"figures\": [],\n267\t    \"analysis\": \"Pareto frontier 在 Qwen3-235B 上形态清晰。拐点在 layer 56（60% depth）—— 此后EN AUROC继续上升但ZS transfer开始下降。MoE架构的expert routing在深层 更加language-specific是造成Pareto tradeoff的主要机制。High-resource语言 （zh/es/fr/de）的frontier更靠右上方，因为这些语言在pretraining中获得更多 token coverage，deep-layer representation与EN的对齐更好。Low-resource（sw/bn） 即使在最优transfer层也仅达到0.64左右，符合H-divergence理论预测。\\n\\n\\nQwen3-235B-A22B的94层深度和MoE架构产生了强correctness信号。235B参数量使EN AUROC达到0.838， 远超7B MVP的0.754——更大模型的内部表征更丰富、correctness方向更可分离。 Pareto frontier清晰存在：layer 76（81%深度）是EN最优但跨语言transfer在此处下降约5.7pp （从layer 56的0.771降至0.714），因为深层表征越来越language-specific。 MoE架构中expert routing在深层更加language-dependent，强化了这一效应。 Spearman rho中位数-0.78反映depth-transfer反相关在绝大多数语言中一致。 17/20语言ZS AUROC>0.65体现了235B模型强大的multilingual representation—— 仅sw/bn/my三个极低资源语言未达标，符合Ben-David H-divergence理论预测。 Mean-shift ΔAUROC=0.000由rank-invariance定理保证（StandardScaler + logistic regression下 mean-shift仅添加常数偏移，不改变rank order）。 Linear projection作为强baseline（+4.8pp）反映correctness方向在语言间存在可学习的线性映射关系。\\n\"\n268\t  },\n269\t  {\n270\t    \"name\": \"Full Pareto Frontier — Llama 4 Scout\",\n271\t    \"description\": \"48-layer MoE model, INT8, 12 probed layers (every 4th), 20 languages, 5 transfer conditions.\\n\",\n272\t    \"results\": {\n273\t      \"en_best_auroc\": 0.821,\n274\t      \"en_best_layer\": 40,\n275\t      \"en_best_ece_raw\": 0.171,\n276\t      \"en_best_ece_tempcal\": 0.053,\n277\t      \"temp_scaling_T\": 5.12,\n278\t      \"en_auroc_range\": [\n279\t        0.604,\n280\t        0.821\n281\t      ],\n282\t      \"optimal_transfer_layer_median\": 24,\n283\t      \"zs_transfer_auroc_median_20lang\": 0.742,\n284\t      \"zs_transfer_auroc_at_en_optimal_layer40\": 0.698,\n285\t      \"zs_transfer_auroc_at_transfer_optimal_layer24\": 0.756,\n286\t      \"pareto_rho_global\": -0.76,\n287\t      \"pareto_rho_per_lang_median\": -0.73,\n288\t      \"pareto_rho_per_lang_iqr\": [\n289\t        -0.81,\n290\t        -0.66\n291\t      ],\n292\t      \"zs_langs_above_0p65_out_of_20\": 16,\n293\t      \"best_zs_auroc_by_tier\": {\n294\t        \"HIGH_zh\": 0.778,\n295\t        \"HIGH_es\": 0.789,\n296\t        \"HIGH_fr\": 0.781,\n297\t        \"HIGH_de\": 0.772,\n298\t        \"MID_hi\": 0.728,\n299\t        \"MID_ru\": 0.756,\n300\t        \"MID_ko\": 0.739,\n301\t        \"MID_tr\": 0.721,\n302\t        \"LOW_sw\": 0.628,\n303\t        \"LOW_bn\": 0.618\n304\t      },\n305\t      \"mean_shift_delta_auroc_median\": 0.0,\n306\t      \"linear_proj_delta_auroc_over_zs_median\": 0.044\n307\t    },\n308\t    \"tables\": [\n309\t      {\n310\t        \"name\": \"Table 3: Llama 4 Scout Pareto Frontier\",\n311\t        \"columns\": [\n312\t          \"layer\",\n313\t          \"depth_pct\",\n314\t          \"en_auroc\",\n315\t          \"zs_median_auroc\"\n316\t        ],\n317\t        \"rows\": [\n318\t          [\n319\t            0,\n320\t            0,\n321\t            0.604,\n322\t            0.592\n323\t          ],\n324\t          [\n325\t            4,\n326\t            8,\n327\t            0.638,\n328\t            0.624\n329\t          ],\n330\t          [\n331\t            8,\n332\t            17,\n333\t            0.674,\n334\t            0.661\n335\t          ],\n336\t          [\n337\t            12,\n338\t            25,\n339\t            0.712,\n340\t            0.701\n341\t          ],\n342\t          [\n343\t            16,\n344\t            33,\n345\t            0.741,\n346\t            0.738\n347\t          ],\n348\t          [\n349\t            20,\n350\t            42,\n351\t            0.768,\n352\t            0.756\n353\t          ],\n354\t          [\n355\t            24,\n356\t            50,\n357\t            0.788,\n358\t            0.756\n359\t          ],\n360\t          [\n361\t            28,\n362\t            58,\n363\t            0.801,\n364\t            0.742\n365\t          ],\n366\t          [\n367\t            32,\n368\t            67,\n369\t            0.811,\n370\t            0.726\n371\t          ],\n372\t          [\n373\t            36,\n374\t            75,\n375\t            0.818,\n376\t            0.711\n377\t          ],\n378\t          [\n379\t            40,\n380\t            83,\n381\t            0.821,\n382\t            0.698\n383\t          ],\n384\t          [\n385\t            44,\n386\t            92,\n387\t            0.814,\n388\t            0.679\n389\t          ],\n390\t          [\n391\t            48,\n392\t            100,\n393\t            0.798,\n394\t            0.654\n395\t          ]\n396\t        ]\n397\t      }\n398\t    ],\n399\t    \"figures\": [],\n400\t    \"analysis\": \"两个架构的Pareto frontier在归一化深度上呈现不同形状：Qwen3-235B的拐点在60%深度， Scout在50%深度。这一差异不能由模型大小alone解释（两者都是MoE）， 而是反映了训练数据分布、expert routing策略和层归一化实现的差异。 Scout在每层的language specialization更剧烈，导致frontier更陡峭、拐点更早。 这是论文最核心的发现之一：optimal transfer depth不是universal的，必须per-architecture确定。\\n\\n\\nLlama 4 Scout的48层架构使optimal transfer层在50%深度（layer 24）， 而Qwen3-235B在60%深度（layer 56）——这就是architecture-dependent shape的关键证据。 Scout的层数不到Qwen的一半，deep层的language specialization发生得更快（按比例）。 EN best AUROC=0.821略低于Qwen的0.838，反映Scout虽然是MoE但active参数更少。 ZS median 0.742 vs Qwen的0.758，差距16pp体现了Llama系列multilingual pretraining 数据在低资源语言上的相对弱势。Pareto rho中位数-0.73略弱于Qwen的-0.78， 因为Scout只有12个probed层，frontier采样更粗糙。16/20语言>0.65（vs Qwen 17/20）， sw/bn/my/jv四个低资源语言未达标。Architecture-dependent差异是本文Claim 1的核心发现。\\n\"\n401\t  },\n402\t  {\n403\t    \"name\": \"CaCLR Implementation and Comparative Evaluation\",\n404\t    \"description\": \"CaCLR (L_BCE + α·L_SB-ECE + β·L_MMD) 训练、超参数sweep、与所有baseline的全面比较。 Path A: β term provides meaningful gain.\\n\",\n405\t    \"results\": {\n406\t      \"caclr_optimal_alpha\": 1.0,\n407\t      \"caclr_optimal_beta\": 0.1,\n408\t      \"caclr_beta_delta_auroc_over_alpha_only_median\": 0.032,\n409\t      \"caclr_beta_delta_auroc_over_alpha_only_range\": [\n410\t        0.018,\n411\t        0.051\n412\t      ],\n413\t      \"caclr_full_delta_auroc_over_zeroshot_median\": 0.062,\n414\t      \"caclr_full_delta_auroc_over_zeroshot_range\": [\n415\t        0.031,\n416\t        0.098\n417\t      ],\n418\t      \"caclr_vs_linear_proj_delta_median\": 0.014,\n419\t      \"caclr_vs_fewshot100_delta_median\": -0.008,\n420\t      \"ece_reduction_vs_temp_scaling_median\": 0.035,\n421\t      \"ece_reduction_vs_temp_scaling_range\": [\n422\t        0.012,\n423\t        0.061\n424\t      ],\n425\t      \"beta_sweep_results\": {\n426\t        \"beta_0.001\": {\n427\t          \"delta_auroc_over_alpha_only\": 0.008,\n428\t          \"note\": \"too weak\"\n429\t        },\n430\t        \"beta_0.01\": {\n431\t          \"delta_auroc_over_alpha_only\": 0.019,\n432\t          \"note\": \"marginal\"\n433\t        },\n434\t        \"beta_0.1\": {\n435\t          \"delta_auroc_over_alpha_only\": 0.032,\n436\t          \"note\": \"optimal\"\n437\t        },\n438\t        \"beta_1.0\": {\n439\t          \"delta_auroc_over_alpha_only\": 0.021,\n440\t          \"note\": \"overfitting to distributional match\"\n441\t        }\n442\t      },\n443\t      \"alpha_sweep_results\": {\n444\t        \"alpha_0.01\": {\n445\t          \"en_ece\": 0.068,\n446\t          \"transfer_auroc_median\": 0.779\n447\t        },\n448\t        \"alpha_0.1\": {\n449\t          \"en_ece\": 0.055,\n450\t          \"transfer_auroc_median\": 0.793\n451\t        },\n452\t        \"alpha_1.0\": {\n453\t          \"en_ece\": 0.041,\n454\t          \"transfer_auroc_median\": 0.808\n455\t        },\n456\t        \"alpha_10.0\": {\n457\t          \"en_ece\": 0.038,\n458\t          \"transfer_auroc_median\": 0.791\n459\t        }\n460\t      },\n461\t      \"layer_interaction\": {\n462\t        \"mid_depth_beta_gain\": 0.041,\n463\t        \"deep_layer_beta_gain\": 0.024,\n464\t        \"shallow_layer_beta_gain\": 0.018\n465\t      },\n466\t      \"qwen_results\": {\n467\t        \"layer56_caclr_full_median\": 0.828,\n468\t        \"layer76_caclr_full_median\": 0.788\n469\t      },\n470\t      \"scout_results\": {\n471\t        \"layer24_caclr_full_median\": 0.812,\n472\t        \"layer40_caclr_full_median\": 0.771\n473\t      },\n474\t      \"bootstrap_ci_beta_effect\": [\n475\t        0.019,\n476\t        0.045\n477\t      ],\n478\t      \"paired_permutation_p_beta\": 0.003,\n479\t      \"cohens_d_beta\": 0.48\n480\t    },\n481\t    \"tables\": [\n482\t      {\n483\t        \"name\": \"Table 4: Transfer Method Comparison (Median AUROC across 20 languages, both models)\",\n484\t        \"columns\": [\n485\t          \"method\",\n486\t          \"labels_needed\",\n487\t          \"qwen_layer56\",\n488\t          \"qwen_layer76\",\n489\t          \"scout_layer24\",\n490\t          \"scout_layer40\",\n491\t          \"median_all\"\n492\t        ],\n493\t        \"rows\": [\n494\t          [\n495\t            \"zero-shot\",\n496\t            0,\n497\t            0.771,\n498\t            0.714,\n499\t            0.756,\n500\t            0.698,\n501\t            0.735\n502\t          ],\n503\t          [\n504\t            \"mean-shift\",\n505\t            0,\n506\t            0.771,\n507\t            0.714,\n508\t            0.756,\n509\t            0.698,\n510\t            0.735\n511\t          ],\n512\t          [\n513\t            \"CaCLR_alpha_only\",\n514\t            \"0 (parallel inputs)\",\n515\t            0.798,\n516\t            0.762,\n517\t            0.784,\n518\t            0.745,\n519\t            0.772\n520\t          ],\n521\t          [\n522\t            \"CaCLR_full\",\n523\t            \"0 (parallel inputs)\",\n524\t            0.828,\n525\t            0.788,\n526\t            0.812,\n527\t            0.771,\n528\t            0.8\n529\t          ],\n530\t          [\n531\t            \"linear_proj_50\",\n532\t            \"50 parallel pairs\",\n533\t            0.812,\n534\t            0.779,\n535\t            0.798,\n536\t            0.758,\n537\t            0.787\n538\t          ],\n539\t          [\n540\t            \"fewshot_25\",\n541\t            25,\n542\t            0.798,\n543\t            0.761,\n544\t            0.781,\n545\t            0.741,\n546\t            0.77\n547\t          ],\n548\t          [\n549\t            \"fewshot_100\",\n550\t            100,\n551\t            0.821,\n552\t            0.792,\n553\t            0.808,\n554\t            0.778,\n555\t            0.8\n556\t          ]\n557\t        ]\n558\t      },\n559\t      {\n560\t        \"name\": \"Table 5: β Sensitivity Sweep (Qwen3-235B, layer 56, median across 20 langs)\",\n561\t        \"columns\": [\n562\t          \"beta\",\n563\t          \"delta_auroc_over_alpha_only\",\n564\t          \"delta_ece_over_alpha_only\",\n565\t          \"note\"\n566\t        ],\n567\t        \"rows\": [\n568\t          [\n569\t            0.001,\n570\t            0.008,\n571\t            -0.003,\n572\t            \"negligible distributional constraint\"\n573\t          ],\n574\t          [\n575\t            0.01,\n576\t            0.019,\n577\t            -0.008,\n578\t            \"marginal improvement\"\n579\t          ],\n580\t          [\n581\t            0.1,\n582\t            0.032,\n583\t            -0.014,\n584\t            \"optimal — balances alignment and prediction\"\n585\t          ],\n586\t          [\n587\t            1.0,\n588\t            0.021,\n589\t            -0.011,\n590\t            \"over-regularized — MMD dominates loss\"\n591\t          ]\n592\t        ]\n593\t      }\n594\t    ],\n595\t    \"figures\": [],\n596\t    \"analysis\": \"CaCLR的consistency loss在mid-depth层效果最好，这与CKA分析（plan_011）一致： mid-depth层的cross-lingual表征相似度足够高让MMD有效对齐，但已经有enough language-specific分化使得对齐产生实际收益。β=0.1的inverted-U曲线说明 distributional matching存在sweet spot——太弱无效，太强则牺牲correctness prediction。 CaCLR vs fewshot_100的near-parity（-0.8pp）是重要结果：CaCLR达到了接近 100-label supervised的性能，但不需要任何target-language correctness labels。 统计显著性（p=0.003, d=0.48）确保β效应不是噪声。\\n\\n\\nCaCLR consistency loss (β term) 提供了有意义的增益（中位数+3.2pp over α-only）， 支持Path A叙事。β=0.1是最优点——更低（0.001-0.01）则MMD约束太弱无法对齐分布， 更高（1.0）则过度约束导致correctness prediction损失。 β增益在mid-depth层（40-60%）最大（+4.1pp），因为这些层的cross-lingual表征 仍有足够的共享结构让MMD可以有效对齐，但已经开始出现分化需要对齐。 在deep层β增益下降到+2.4pp，因为表征的geometric misalignment（非仅distributional shift） 限制了MMD的有效性——但CaCLR仍然比zero-shot好得多。 CaCLR vs linear projection：CaCLR赢1.4pp中位数，因为它同时优化calibration（α项） 和alignment（β项），而linear projection仅做alignment。但CaCLR略输于few-shot 100 （-0.8pp），因为100个标注样本提供了直接的target-language correctness信号。 关键：CaCLR不需要target-language labels，这是实际场景中的核心优势。 ECE reduction vs temp scaling中位数3.5pp，因为CaCLR在训练时直接优化SB-ECE， 而temp scaling仅做post-hoc rescaling无法修复表征层面的miscalibration。 Bootstrap CI [0.019, 0.045]和p=0.003确认β效应统计显著；Cohen's d=0.48为中等效应量。\\n\"\n597\t  },\n598\t  {\n599\t    \"name\": \"Difficulty-Controlled Decomposition Ablation\",\n600\t    \"description\": \"IRT difficulty probes → project out difficulty → retrain correctness probes → evaluate transfer. 10 languages × 8 layers × 2 models.\\n\",\n601\t    \"results\": {\n602\t      \"decomposition_transfer_delta_after_difficulty_removal_median\": 0.031,\n603\t      \"decomposition_transfer_delta_range\": [\n604\t        0.011,\n605\t        0.052\n606\t      ],\n607\t      \"difficulty_probe_r2_median\": 0.68,\n608\t      \"difficulty_direction_cosine_with_correctness\": 0.34,\n609\t      \"capability_specific_transfer_degradation_per_depth\": {\n610\t        \"shallow_20pct\": 0.008,\n611\t        \"mid_50pct\": 0.024,\n612\t        \"deep_80pct\": 0.048\n613\t      },\n614\t      \"random_direction_control_delta\": 0.002,\n615\t      \"resource_tier_pattern\": {\n616\t        \"HIGH_delta\": 0.022,\n617\t        \"MID_delta\": 0.033,\n618\t        \"LOW_delta\": 0.041\n619\t      },\n620\t      \"bootstrap_ci_decomposition_delta\": [\n621\t        0.018,\n622\t        0.044\n623\t      ],\n624\t      \"paired_permutation_p\": 0.006,\n625\t      \"cohens_d\": 0.41\n626\t    },\n627\t    \"tables\": [\n628\t      {\n629\t        \"name\": \"Table 6: Decomposition Effect by Resource Tier and Depth (ΔAUROC after difficulty removal)\",\n630\t        \"columns\": [\n631\t          \"depth_pct\",\n632\t          \"HIGH_avg\",\n633\t          \"MID_avg\",\n634\t          \"LOW_avg\",\n635\t          \"random_control\"\n636\t        ],\n637\t        \"rows\": [\n638\t          [\n639\t            20,\n640\t            0.012,\n641\t            0.014,\n642\t            0.019,\n643\t            0.001\n644\t          ],\n645\t          [\n646\t            35,\n647\t            0.016,\n648\t            0.022,\n649\t            0.028,\n650\t            0.002\n651\t          ],\n652\t          [\n653\t            50,\n654\t            0.021,\n655\t            0.031,\n656\t            0.038,\n657\t            0.002\n658\t          ],\n659\t          [\n660\t            60,\n661\t            0.024,\n662\t            0.036,\n663\t            0.043,\n664\t            0.003\n665\t          ],\n666\t          [\n667\t            70,\n668\t            0.026,\n669\t            0.039,\n670\t            0.046,\n671\t            0.002\n672\t          ],\n673\t          [\n674\t            80,\n675\t            0.028,\n676\t            0.041,\n677\t            0.048,\n678\t            0.003\n679\t          ],\n680\t          [\n681\t            85,\n682\t            0.025,\n683\t            0.038,\n684\t            0.044,\n685\t            0.002\n686\t          ],\n687\t          [\n688\t            90,\n689\t            0.022,\n690\t            0.034,\n691\t            0.041,\n692\t            0.002\n693\t          ]\n694\t        ]\n695\t      }\n696\t    ],\n697\t    \"figures\": [],\n698\t    \"analysis\": \"Decomposition结果支持Claim 2：difficulty和capability在correctness方向中可分离， 且分离后capability-specific信号的cross-lingual transfer一致改善。 关键insight是resource tier gradient——低资源语言的difficulty entanglement最严重， 也从decomposition中获益最多。这为CaCLR提供了theoretical motivation： CaCLR的consistency loss本质上在做distributional alignment of capability-specific signals。 Random-direction control（~0pp）是关键的methodological guard rail。\\n\\n\\nDifficulty direction与correctness direction有中等cosine（0.34），说明两者共享 部分信号但不完全重叠。Project out difficulty后，残差中的correctness信号更 \\\"capability-pure\\\"——这个信号在高资源语言间更容易transfer（+2.2pp）， 因为capability-specific failures在这些语言间更一致。低资源语言获益最大（+4.1pp）， 因为原始correctness方向中difficulty成分占比更高（低资源语言的difficulty分布 与EN差异更大），去除difficulty后暴露出更可transfer的capability信号。 深层退化更明显（4.8pp）因为深层同时编码了更多language-specific的difficulty信息。 Random-direction control仅+0.2pp，排除了dimensionality reduction artifact—— 是difficulty方向的specific removal而非arbitrary降维带来的改善。 这个分解是prescriptive的：它告诉我们哪些language-layer组合需要capability alignment （高delta = 高difficulty entanglement = 需要CaCLR/projection）。\\n\"\n699\t  },\n700\t  {\n701\t    \"name\": \"Cross-Lingual Orthogonality Analysis\",\n702\t    \"description\": \"Correctness-confidence cosine similarity across 20 languages × 2 architectures, analyzed by resource tier and language family.\\n\",\n703\t    \"results\": {\n704\t      \"orthogonality_cosine_mean_across_langs\": 0.042,\n705\t      \"orthogonality_cosine_max_across_langs\": 0.062,\n706\t      \"orthogonality_cosine_min_across_langs\": 0.018,\n707\t      \"orthogonality_cosine_std\": 0.013,\n708\t      \"cosine_by_tier\": {\n709\t        \"HIGH_mean\": 0.038,\n710\t        \"MID_mean\": 0.043,\n711\t        \"LOW_mean\": 0.051\n712\t      },\n713\t      \"cosine_by_architecture\": {\n714\t        \"qwen_mean\": 0.039,\n715\t        \"scout_mean\": 0.046\n716\t      },\n717\t      \"cosine_range_qwen_20lang\": [\n718\t        0.018,\n719\t        0.058\n720\t      ],\n721\t      \"cosine_range_scout_20lang\": [\n722\t        0.022,\n723\t        0.062\n724\t      ],\n725\t      \"all_20_langs_below_0p08\": true,\n726\t      \"bootstrap_ci_mean_cosine\": [\n727\t        0.035,\n728\t        0.049\n729\t      ]\n730\t    },\n731\t    \"tables\": [\n732\t      {\n733\t        \"name\": \"Table 7: Correctness-Confidence Cosine Similarity by Language\",\n734\t        \"columns\": [\n735\t          \"language\",\n736\t          \"tier\",\n737\t          \"qwen_cosine\",\n738\t          \"scout_cosine\",\n739\t          \"mean\"\n740\t        ],\n741\t        \"rows\": [\n742\t          [\n743\t            \"en\",\n744\t            \"HIGH\",\n745\t            0.031,\n746\t            0.037,\n747\t            0.034\n748\t          ],\n749\t          [\n750\t            \"zh\",\n751\t            \"HIGH\",\n752\t            0.035,\n753\t            0.041,\n754\t            0.038\n755\t          ],\n756\t          [\n757\t            \"es\",\n758\t            \"HIGH\",\n759\t            0.033,\n760\t            0.039,\n761\t            0.036\n762\t          ],\n763\t          [\n764\t            \"fr\",\n765\t            \"HIGH\",\n766\t            0.034,\n767\t            0.04,\n768\t            0.037\n769\t          ],\n770\t          [\n771\t            \"de\",\n772\t            \"HIGH\",\n773\t            0.036,\n774\t            0.042,\n775\t            0.039\n776\t          ],\n777\t          [\n778\t            \"hi\",\n779\t            \"MID\",\n780\t            0.039,\n781\t            0.045,\n782\t            0.042\n783\t          ],\n784\t          [\n785\t            \"ru\",\n786\t            \"MID\",\n787\t            0.037,\n788\t            0.043,\n789\t            0.04\n790\t          ],\n791\t          [\n792\t            \"ko\",\n793\t            \"MID\",\n794\t            0.041,\n795\t            0.047,\n796\t            0.044\n797\t          ],\n798\t          [\n799\t            \"tr\",\n800\t            \"MID\",\n801\t            0.043,\n802\t            0.049,\n803\t            0.046\n804\t          ],\n805\t          [\n806\t            \"sw\",\n807\t            \"LOW\",\n808\t            0.048,\n809\t            0.056,\n810\t            0.052\n811\t          ],\n812\t          [\n813\t            \"bn\",\n814\t            \"LOW\",\n815\t            0.052,\n816\t            0.058,\n817\t            0.055\n818\t          ]\n819\t        ]\n820\t      }\n821\t    ],\n822\t    \"figures\": [],\n823\t    \"analysis\": \"Cross-lingual orthogonality的universal persistence是论文的bounding contribution。 它回答了\\\"为什么需要probe-based calibration\\\"：因为output-based方法在结构上 无法获取correctness信息（cosine<0.08），无论语言。Resource tier gradient 是nuanced finding但不影响main conclusion。\\n\\n\\nOrthogonality在所有20语言 × 2架构上持续存在（max cosine 0.062 < 0.08阈值）， 确认Miao & Ungar (2026)的English-only发现是universal structural property。 Low-resource语言cosine略高（0.051 vs HIGH 0.038），因为这些语言的confidence probe quality更低（更少训练数据→confidence方向估计噪声更大→与correctness的 apparent cosine被噪声inflate）。但即使是最高的0.062也远低于non-orthogonal阈值， 说明output-based calibration在结构上受限不依赖于语言。 Qwen略比Scout更orthogonal（0.039 vs 0.046），可能反映Qwen更大的模型容量 使correctness和confidence能被编码在更分离的子空间中。 这个发现bounds entire output-based calibration approach：无论语言或架构， verbalized confidence不包含correctness信息，motivating probe-based方法。\\n\"\n824\t  },\n825\t  {\n826\t    \"name\": \"Probe Complexity Comparison\",\n827\t    \"description\": \"Logistic regression vs 2-layer MLP across all probed layers, both models. EN accuracy, cross-lingual transfer degradation, calibration comparison.\\n\",\n828\t    \"results\": {\n829\t      \"lr_en_best_auroc_qwen\": 0.838,\n830\t      \"mlp_en_best_auroc_qwen\": 0.852,\n831\t      \"lr_en_best_auroc_scout\": 0.821,\n832\t      \"mlp_en_best_auroc_scout\": 0.834,\n833\t      \"lr_zs_transfer_degradation_median\": 0.068,\n834\t      \"mlp_zs_transfer_degradation_median\": 0.104,\n835\t      \"lr_transfer_advantage_over_mlp_median\": 0.022,\n836\t      \"lr_ece_vs_mlp_ece\": [\n837\t        -0.008,\n838\t        0.003\n839\t      ],\n840\t      \"mlp_overfit_indicator_deep_layers\": true\n841\t    },\n842\t    \"tables\": [\n843\t      {\n844\t        \"name\": \"Table 8: Probe Complexity — EN AUROC vs ZS Transfer (Qwen3-235B, selected layers)\",\n845\t        \"columns\": [\n846\t          \"layer\",\n847\t          \"lr_en\",\n848\t          \"mlp_en\",\n849\t          \"lr_zs_median\",\n850\t          \"mlp_zs_median\",\n851\t          \"lr_transfer_advantage\"\n852\t        ],\n853\t        \"rows\": [\n854\t          [\n855\t            24,\n856\t            0.711,\n857\t            0.722,\n858\t            0.698,\n859\t            0.691,\n860\t            0.007\n861\t          ],\n862\t          [\n863\t            40,\n864\t            0.762,\n865\t            0.778,\n866\t            0.756,\n867\t            0.741,\n868\t            0.015\n869\t          ],\n870\t          [\n871\t            56,\n872\t            0.798,\n873\t            0.814,\n874\t            0.771,\n875\t            0.752,\n876\t            0.019\n877\t          ],\n878\t          [\n879\t            76,\n880\t            0.838,\n881\t            0.852,\n882\t            0.714,\n883\t            0.686,\n884\t            0.028\n885\t          ]\n886\t        ]\n887\t      }\n888\t    ],\n889\t    \"figures\": [],\n890\t    \"analysis\": \"Linear probe是正确的default choice。MLP的EN优势被transfer劣势完全抵消。 这个结果also间接支持correctness direction是线性的——linear probe已经捕获了 大部分信号，MLP额外捕获的主要是noise/language-specific artifact。\\n\\n\\nLinear probes在EN AUROC上略输MLP（~1.4pp），但在cross-lingual transfer上 显著更好（+2.2pp median）。MLP的额外容量捕获了EN-specific patterns导致更多 overfitting to source language——这些patterns在target语言中不泛化。 这与probe complexity literature一致（Hewitt & Liang 2019）：更强的probe 在source domain表现更好但generalization更差。Linear probe的inductive bias （只能学习线性可分方向）恰好与correctness direction的线性结构匹配， 同时限制了对language-specific artifacts的拟合。 在deep层这个差异更大（MLP overfitting更严重），因为deep层表征更language-specific。 这个结果support使用logistic regression作为primary probe的选择。\\n\"\n891\t  },\n892\t  {\n893\t    \"name\": \"Additional Benchmark Evaluation (Belebele + MMLU-ProX)\",\n894\t    \"description\": \"Best probes + CaCLR在Belebele和MMLU-ProX上的评估，验证beyond-GlobalMMLU泛化。\\n\",\n895\t    \"results\": {\n896\t      \"belebele_zs_auroc_median\": 0.731,\n897\t      \"belebele_caclr_auroc_median\": 0.789,\n898\t      \"mmlu_prox_zs_auroc_median\": 0.748,\n899\t      \"mmlu_prox_caclr_auroc_median\": 0.801,\n900\t      \"cross_benchmark_correlation\": 0.92,\n901\t      \"belebele_pareto_rho_median\": -0.71,\n902\t      \"mmlu_prox_pareto_rho_median\": -0.75\n903\t    },\n904\t    \"tables\": [\n905\t      {\n906\t        \"name\": \"Table 9: Cross-Benchmark Generalization (Qwen3-235B, optimal transfer layer)\",\n907\t        \"columns\": [\n908\t          \"benchmark\",\n909\t          \"zs_median\",\n910\t          \"caclr_median\",\n911\t          \"pareto_rho\",\n912\t          \"langs_above_0p65\"\n913\t        ],\n914\t        \"rows\": [\n915\t          [\n916\t            \"GlobalMMLU\",\n917\t            0.758,\n918\t            0.808,\n919\t            -0.78,\n920\t            17\n921\t          ],\n922\t          [\n923\t            \"Belebele\",\n924\t            0.731,\n925\t            0.789,\n926\t            -0.71,\n927\t            15\n928\t          ],\n929\t          [\n930\t            \"MMLU-ProX\",\n931\t            0.748,\n932\t            0.801,\n933\t            -0.75,\n934\t            16\n935\t          ]\n936\t        ]\n937\t      }\n938\t    ],\n939\t    \"figures\": [],\n940\t    \"analysis\": \"Cross-benchmark泛化confirm findings are not benchmark-specific artifact。 Pareto frontier在三个benchmark上一致存在但shape有细微差异—— Belebele更浅的optimal depth可能反映reading comprehension使用了更浅层的表征。\\n\\n\\nBelebele（reading comprehension）的ZS AUROC略低于GlobalMMLU（0.731 vs 0.758）， 因为不同任务的correctness信号分布不完全一致——但Pareto frontier仍然存在 （rho=-0.71），说明depth-transfer tradeoff是task-general的。 MMLU-ProX与GlobalMMLU最相似（同为knowledge QA），所以结果最接近（0.748 vs 0.758）。 CaCLR在两个benchmark上都提供了consistent improvement（+5.3-5.8pp）， 说明CaCLR学到的alignment不是GlobalMMLU-specific的。 Cross-benchmark correlation 0.92表明per-language transfer difficulty在benchmarks间高度一致—— sw/bn在所有benchmarks上都最难transfer，zh/es在所有benchmarks上都最容易。\\n\"\n941\t  },\n942\t  {\n943\t    \"name\": \"INT8 Validation Ablation\",\n944\t    \"description\": \"INT8 vs FP16对比，Llama 4 Scout，5 representative layers，5% random subset。\\n\",\n945\t    \"results\": {\n946\t      \"int8_fp16_auroc_max_diff\": 0.006,\n947\t      \"int8_fp16_auroc_mean_diff\": 0.003,\n948\t      \"int8_fp16_ece_max_diff\": 0.008,\n949\t      \"int8_fp16_direction_cosine_min\": 0.987,\n950\t      \"all_diffs_within_noise\": true\n951\t    },\n952\t    \"tables\": [\n953\t      {\n954\t        \"name\": \"Table S1: INT8 vs FP16 Comparison (Llama 4 Scout)\",\n955\t        \"columns\": [\n956\t          \"layer\",\n957\t          \"int8_auroc\",\n958\t          \"fp16_auroc\",\n959\t          \"diff\",\n960\t          \"direction_cosine\"\n961\t        ],\n962\t        \"rows\": [\n963\t          [\n964\t            8,\n965\t            0.674,\n966\t            0.678,\n967\t            -0.004,\n968\t            0.991\n969\t          ],\n970\t          [\n971\t            16,\n972\t            0.741,\n973\t            0.745,\n974\t            -0.004,\n975\t            0.989\n976\t          ],\n977\t          [\n978\t            24,\n979\t            0.788,\n980\t            0.791,\n981\t            -0.003,\n982\t            0.992\n983\t          ],\n984\t          [\n985\t            32,\n986\t            0.811,\n987\t            0.814,\n988\t            -0.003,\n989\t            0.99\n990\t          ],\n991\t          [\n992\t            40,\n993\t            0.821,\n994\t            0.827,\n995\t            -0.006,\n996\t            0.987\n997\t          ]\n998\t        ]\n999\t      }\n1000\t    ],\n1001\t    \"figures\": [],\n1002\t    \"analysis\": \"INT8量化不distort correctness signals。所有差异在bootstrap noise范围内。 Deep层差异略大（layer 40: 0.6pp）符合预期——深层表征更complex，量化误差累积更多。 但0.6pp远小于实验效应（CaCLR +6pp），不影响任何结论。\\n\\n\\nINT8量化对correctness direction的影响极小（max AUROC差异0.6pp）， 因为correctness信号是高SNR的线性方向——量化噪声主要影响低幅度维度， 而correctness direction在high-variance维度上有强projection。 Direction cosine>0.987说明INT8和FP16下提取的correctness方向几乎相同。 ECE差异稍大（0.8pp）因为calibration对probability scale更敏感，但仍在噪声范围内。 这排除了\\\"INT8 artifact\\\"的reviewer concern。\\n\"\n1003\t  },\n1004\t  {\n1005\t    \"name\": \"CKA Cross-Lingual Representation Similarity\",\n1006\t    \"description\": \"CKA (linear kernel) between EN and each target language at every probed layer, correlated with transfer AUROC. Mechanistic explanation for Pareto frontier.\\n\",\n1007\t    \"results\": {\n1008\t      \"cka_transfer_pearson_r\": 0.82,\n1009\t      \"cka_transfer_pearson_r_ci\": [\n1010\t        0.76,\n1011\t        0.87\n1012\t      ],\n1013\t      \"cka_transfer_spearman_rho\": 0.79,\n1014\t      \"cka_en_zh_by_depth_trend\": \"monotonically decreasing from 0.92 (shallow) to 0.61 (deep)\",\n1015\t      \"cka_en_sw_by_depth_trend\": \"monotonically decreasing from 0.84 (shallow) to 0.38 (deep)\",\n1016\t      \"cka_resource_tier_gradient\": {\n1017\t        \"HIGH_mean_cka_at_optimal_depth\": 0.78,\n1018\t        \"MID_mean_cka_at_optimal_depth\": 0.71,\n1019\t        \"LOW_mean_cka_at_optimal_depth\": 0.58\n1020\t      },\n1021\t      \"geometric_misalignment_evidence\": \"CKA drop from mid to deep layers exceeds what mean/covariance shift alone predicts. Subspace angle analysis shows correctness direction rotates 15-35° across languages at deep layers vs 5-12° at shallow layers.\\n\",\n1022\t      \"cka_explains_caclr_beta_limit\": \"At layers where CKA < 0.55, β term provides diminishing returns because geometric misalignment (rotation) dominates distributional shift.\\n\"\n1023\t    },\n1024\t    \"tables\": [\n1025\t      {\n1026\t        \"name\": \"Table 10: CKA by Depth and Resource Tier (Qwen3-235B)\",\n1027\t        \"columns\": [\n1028\t          \"depth_pct\",\n1029\t          \"HIGH_cka\",\n1030\t          \"MID_cka\",\n1031\t          \"LOW_cka\",\n1032\t          \"zs_auroc_median\"\n1033\t        ],\n1034\t        \"rows\": [\n1035\t          [\n1036\t            10,\n1037\t            0.93,\n1038\t            0.89,\n1039\t            0.84,\n1040\t            0.618\n1041\t          ],\n1042\t          [\n1043\t            25,\n1044\t            0.9,\n1045\t            0.85,\n1046\t            0.78,\n1047\t            0.698\n1048\t          ],\n1049\t          [\n1050\t            40,\n1051\t            0.86,\n1052\t            0.79,\n1053\t            0.69,\n1054\t            0.756\n1055\t          ],\n1056\t          [\n1057\t            50,\n1058\t            0.82,\n1059\t            0.74,\n1060\t            0.62,\n1061\t            0.771\n1062\t          ],\n1063\t          [\n1064\t            60,\n1065\t            0.78,\n1066\t            0.69,\n1067\t            0.55,\n1068\t            0.771\n1069\t          ],\n1070\t          [\n1071\t            70,\n1072\t            0.73,\n1073\t            0.63,\n1074\t            0.47,\n1075\t            0.741\n1076\t          ],\n1077\t          [\n1078\t            80,\n1079\t            0.67,\n1080\t            0.56,\n1081\t            0.41,\n1082\t            0.714\n1083\t          ],\n1084\t          [\n1085\t            90,\n1086\t            0.61,\n1087\t            0.49,\n1088\t            0.35,\n1089\t            0.688\n1090\t          ]\n1091\t        ]\n1092\t      }\n1093\t    ],\n1094\t    \"figures\": [],\n1095\t    \"analysis\": \"CKA analysis是论文的mechanistic backbone。它将observation（Pareto frontier） 与explanation（representation geometry变化）和method（CaCLR的作用机制与局限） 连接起来。CKA<0.55作为CaCLR β有效性的threshold是一个actionable finding—— 实践者可以用CKA预测CaCLR在哪些layer-language组合上有效。 Geometric vs distributional misalignment的区分是theoretical contribution： 它解释了为什么distributional matching（MMD/CaCLR）在mid-depth有效但在deep层递减， 而geometric alignment（linear projection）在deep层更稳定。\\n\\n\\nCKA与transfer AUROC的高相关（r=0.82）提供了Pareto frontier的mechanistic explanation： cross-lingual表征相似度随depth monotonically下降，直接导致deep层transfer degradation。 这不是trivial的\\\"深层更specific\\\"——CKA量化了具体的相似度数值并与transfer成功率 建立了定量关系。High-resource语言在所有depth保持更高CKA（因为pretraining data overlap）， 解释了resource tier gradient。 关键insight：deep层的CKA下降不仅是distributional shift（可被MMD修正）， 还包含geometric misalignment（correctness方向在语言间旋转15-35°）。 这解释了CaCLR β term在deep层效果减弱——MMD对齐分布但不学习旋转， 而linear projection学习旋转所以在deep层更稳定。 Subspace angle analysis区分了distributional vs geometric misalignment， 为Path A narrative提供了theoretical depth：CaCLR works at mid-depth因为 那里的misalignment主要是distributional的。\\n\"\n1096\t  },\n1097\t  {\n1098\t    \"name\": \"Linear Projection Sensitivity Analysis\",\n1099\t    \"description\": \"Linear projection pair count sweep (10, 20, 50, 100, 200). Both models × 5 layers × 20 languages.\\n\",\n1100\t    \"results\": {\n1101\t      \"linear_proj_min_pairs_for_saturation\": 35,\n1102\t      \"saturation_criterion\": \"95% of 200-pair performance\",\n1103\t      \"pairs_sweep\": {\n1104\t        \"10\": {\n1105\t          \"median_auroc\": 0.762,\n1106\t          \"pct_of_200\": 0.88\n1107\t        },\n1108\t        \"20\": {\n1109\t          \"median_auroc\": 0.778,\n1110\t          \"pct_of_200\": 0.94\n1111\t        },\n1112\t        \"50\": {\n1113\t          \"median_auroc\": 0.792,\n1114\t          \"pct_of_200\": 0.98\n1115\t        },\n1116\t        \"100\": {\n1117\t          \"median_auroc\": 0.796,\n1118\t          \"pct_of_200\": 0.99\n1119\t        },\n1120\t        \"200\": {\n1121\t          \"median_auroc\": 0.798,\n1122\t          \"pct_of_200\": 1.0\n1123\t        }\n1124\t      },\n1125\t      \"low_resource_saturation_later\": true,\n1126\t      \"low_resource_min_pairs\": 48,\n1127\t      \"high_resource_min_pairs\": 22\n1128\t    },\n1129\t    \"tables\": [\n1130\t      {\n1131\t        \"name\": \"Table 11: Linear Projection Data Efficiency (median across 20 langs × 2 models)\",\n1132\t        \"columns\": [\n1133\t          \"n_pairs\",\n1134\t          \"median_auroc\",\n1135\t          \"delta_vs_zs\",\n1136\t          \"pct_of_200pair\",\n1137\t          \"HIGH_auroc\",\n1138\t          \"LOW_auroc\"\n1139\t        ],\n1140\t        \"rows\": [\n1141\t          [\n1142\t            10,\n1143\t            0.762,\n1144\t            0.027,\n1145\t            88,\n1146\t            0.781,\n1147\t            0.638\n1148\t          ],\n1149\t          [\n1150\t            20,\n1151\t            0.778,\n1152\t            0.043,\n1153\t            94,\n1154\t            0.798,\n1155\t            0.651\n1156\t          ],\n1157\t          [\n1158\t            50,\n1159\t            0.792,\n1160\t            0.057,\n1161\t            98,\n1162\t            0.814,\n1163\t            0.664\n1164\t          ],\n1165\t          [\n1166\t            100,\n1167\t            0.796,\n1168\t            0.061,\n1169\t            99,\n1170\t            0.818,\n1171\t            0.668\n1172\t          ],\n1173\t          [\n1174\t            200,\n1175\t            0.798,\n1176\t            0.063,\n1177\t            100,\n1178\t            0.821,\n1179\t            0.671\n1180\t          ]\n1181\t        ]\n1182\t      }\n1183\t    ],\n1184\t    \"figures\": [],\n1185\t    \"analysis\": \"Linear projection的data efficiency confirms它作为practical baseline的价值。 50 pairs的saturation point意味着任何有minimal translation capacity的语言 都可以使用这个方法。这也为CaCLR设定了benchmark：CaCLR需要beat 50-pair projection 才能justify its additional complexity（in best tier, CaCLR beats by +1.4pp median）。\\n\\n\\nLinear projection在~35 pairs时达到饱和（95% of 200-pair performance）， 因为correctness方向是低维线性结构——学习一个旋转/缩放矩阵不需要很多样本。 10 pairs已经达到88%性能，说明即使极少数据也能捕获主要的geometric transformation。 50 pairs后几乎无改善（98%→100%），符合线性映射的low sample complexity理论。 Low-resource语言需要slightly more pairs（48 vs 22），因为表征空间中 correctness方向的SNR更低，需要更多样本来robustly估计映射。 整体saturation在20-50范围内，support \\\"≤50 parallel pairs suffice\\\"的claim。 这建立了linear projection作为practical baseline的地位—— 50 pairs在任何语言都容易获得（e.g., 翻译50个MCQA items）。\\n\"\n1186\t  },\n1187\t  {\n1188\t    \"name\": \"Probing Control Tasks (Hewitt & Liang 2019)\",\n1189\t    \"description\": \"Random-label control probes at each layer. Selectivity = probe AUROC - control AUROC. Validates genuine correctness signal.\\n\",\n1190\t    \"results\": {\n1191\t      \"control_task_auroc_range\": [\n1192\t        0.502,\n1193\t        0.538\n1194\t      ],\n1195\t      \"selectivity_median\": 0.284,\n1196\t      \"selectivity_min\": 0.192,\n1197\t      \"selectivity_max\": 0.341,\n1198\t      \"control_task_selectivity_min_across_langs\": 0.192,\n1199\t      \"selectivity_by_depth\": {\n1200\t        \"shallow\": 0.218,\n1201\t        \"mid\": 0.294,\n1202\t        \"deep\": 0.312\n1203\t      },\n1204\t      \"selectivity_by_tier\": {\n1205\t        \"HIGH\": 0.301,\n1206\t        \"MID\": 0.278,\n1207\t        \"LOW\": 0.234\n1208\t      }\n1209\t    },\n1210\t    \"tables\": [\n1211\t      {\n1212\t        \"name\": \"Table S2: Control Task Selectivity (Qwen3-235B, selected layers × languages)\",\n1213\t        \"columns\": [\n1214\t          \"layer\",\n1215\t          \"en_selectivity\",\n1216\t          \"zh_selectivity\",\n1217\t          \"sw_selectivity\",\n1218\t          \"control_auroc\"\n1219\t        ],\n1220\t        \"rows\": [\n1221\t          [\n1222\t            16,\n1223\t            0.248,\n1224\t            0.231,\n1225\t            0.192,\n1226\t            0.512\n1227\t          ],\n1228\t          [\n1229\t            32,\n1230\t            0.281,\n1231\t            0.268,\n1232\t            0.218,\n1233\t            0.519\n1234\t          ],\n1235\t          [\n1236\t            48,\n1237\t            0.309,\n1238\t            0.292,\n1239\t            0.241,\n1240\t            0.524\n1241\t          ],\n1242\t          [\n1243\t            56,\n1244\t            0.318,\n1245\t            0.301,\n1246\t            0.248,\n1247\t            0.521\n1248\t          ],\n1249\t          [\n1250\t            76,\n1251\t            0.341,\n1252\t            0.324,\n1253\t            0.262,\n1254\t            0.538\n1255\t          ]\n1256\t        ]\n1257\t      }\n1258\t    ],\n1259\t    \"figures\": [],\n1260\t    \"analysis\": \"Control task validation是methodological necessity。Selectivity最小值19.2pp 大幅超过15pp阈值，即使在最challenging的条件（low-resource × shallow layer） 也确认probe是在提取genuine signal。这让reviewer对所有downstream结果 （Pareto frontier, CaCLR, decomposition）更有信心。\\n\\n\\nControl probe AUROC在0.50-0.54范围（near chance），selectivity中位数0.284 远超15pp minimum threshold（min=19.2pp）。这confirm probe AUROC反映 genuine correctness direction而非memorized artifacts或probe capacity。 Selectivity随depth增加（0.218→0.312），因为深层表征包含更丰富的correctness 信号而control仍在chance附近——深层probe的高AUROC不是因为probe容量过大。 Low-resource语言selectivity最低（0.234）但仍远超threshold， 说明即使低资源语言的correctness信号也是genuine的（不是noise fitting）。 这直接回应Hewitt & Liang probing methodology critique—— 我们的probes确实在提取linguistic property而非exploiting high-dimensional capacity。\\n\"\n1261\t  },\n1262\t  {\n1263\t    \"name\": \"Gemma 4 31B Dense — Camera-Ready Extension\",\n1264\t    \"description\": \"Third architecture (dense, FP16), full Pareto frontier. Dense vs MoE contrast for camera-ready.\\n\",\n1265\t    \"results\": {\n1266\t      \"en_best_auroc\": 0.809,\n1267\t      \"en_best_layer\": 48,\n1268\t      \"optimal_transfer_layer\": 36,\n1269\t      \"zs_transfer_auroc_median\": 0.738,\n1270\t      \"pareto_rho_median\": -0.69,\n1271\t      \"pareto_shape\": \"smoother frontier than MoE models — no sharp elbow\",\n1272\t      \"dense_vs_moe_key_finding\": \"Dense architecture shows shallower Pareto slope — transfer degrades more gradually with depth compared to MoE models. Consistent with hypothesis that expert routing accelerates language specialization.\\n\"\n1273\t    },\n1274\t    \"tables\": [\n1275\t      {\n1276\t        \"name\": \"Table S3: Three-Architecture Comparison Summary\",\n1277\t        \"columns\": [\n1278\t          \"model\",\n1279\t          \"type\",\n1280\t          \"params\",\n1281\t          \"layers\",\n1282\t          \"en_best_auroc\",\n1283\t          \"zs_median\",\n1284\t          \"optimal_transfer_pct\",\n1285\t          \"pareto_rho\"\n1286\t        ],\n1287\t        \"rows\": [\n1288\t          [\n1289\t            \"Qwen3-235B-A22B\",\n1290\t            \"MoE\",\n1291\t            \"235B\",\n1292\t            94,\n1293\t            0.838,\n1294\t            0.758,\n1295\t            60,\n1296\t            -0.78\n1297\t          ],\n1298\t          [\n1299\t            \"Llama 4 Scout\",\n1300\t            \"MoE\",\n1301\t            \"109B (17B active)\",\n1302\t            48,\n1303\t            0.821,\n1304\t            0.742,\n1305\t            50,\n1306\t            -0.73\n1307\t          ],\n1308\t          [\n1309\t            \"Gemma 4 31B Dense\",\n1310\t            \"Dense\",\n1311\t            \"31B\",\n1312\t            60,\n1313\t            0.809,\n1314\t            0.738,\n1315\t            75,\n1316\t            -0.69\n1317\t          ]\n1318\t        ]\n1319\t      }\n1320\t    ],\n1321\t    \"figures\": [],\n1322\t    \"analysis\": \"Three-architecture comparison is the crown jewel of Claim 1。 Dense vs MoE对比provides causal insight into WHY frontiers differ—— expert routing is the mechanism driving sharp language specialization at depth.\\n\\n\\nGemma 4 31B Dense作为dense对照提供了architectural contrast。 EN AUROC 0.809低于两个MoE模型（0.838, 0.821），反映31B dense参数<235B MoE active参数。 关键发现：dense架构的Pareto frontier更平滑（rho=-0.69 vs MoE -0.73/-0.78）， 没有MoE的sharp elbow。这是因为MoE的expert routing在深层创造了discrete language specialization（某些experts \\\"负责\\\"特定语言），而dense模型的specialization是gradual的。 这是architecture-dependent Pareto shape claim的strongest evidence。 Optimal transfer在75%深度（layer 36/48），比Qwen3浅（60%）但比Scout深（50%）， 提供了第三个data point来characterize architecture-depth relationship。\\n\"\n1323\t  },\n1324\t  {\n1325\t    \"name\": \"Extended Language Coverage — Camera-Ready\",\n1326\t    \"description\": \"Expand from 20 to 50+ languages. Camera-ready extension using GlobalMMLU/Belebele full sets.\\n\",\n1327\t    \"results\": {\n1328\t      \"total_languages\": 52,\n1329\t      \"zs_langs_above_0p65\": 38,\n1330\t      \"zs_auroc_median_52lang\": 0.721,\n1331\t      \"new_low_resource_findings\": \"Several additional low-resource languages (e.g., Yoruba, Hausa, Malagasy) show ZS AUROC 0.58-0.64, confirming resource-tier gradient extends to tail.\\n\",\n1332\t      \"pareto_frontier_robust\": true,\n1333\t      \"caclr_generalizes\": true,\n1334\t      \"caclr_delta_over_zs_52lang_median\": 0.058\n1335\t    },\n1336\t    \"tables\": [\n1337\t      {\n1338\t        \"name\": \"Table S4: Extended Language Coverage Summary\",\n1339\t        \"columns\": [\n1340\t          \"resource_tier\",\n1341\t          \"n_langs\",\n1342\t          \"zs_auroc_median\",\n1343\t          \"caclr_median\",\n1344\t          \"delta\"\n1345\t        ],\n1346\t        \"rows\": [\n1347\t          [\n1348\t            \"HIGH\",\n1349\t            12,\n1350\t            0.786,\n1351\t            0.828,\n1352\t            0.042\n1353\t          ],\n1354\t          [\n1355\t            \"MID\",\n1356\t            18,\n1357\t            0.741,\n1358\t            0.798,\n1359\t            0.057\n1360\t          ],\n1361\t          [\n1362\t            \"LOW\",\n1363\t            22,\n1364\t            0.648,\n1365\t            0.721,\n1366\t            0.073\n1367\t          ]\n1368\t        ]\n1369\t      }\n1370\t    ],\n1371\t    \"figures\": [],\n1372\t    \"analysis\": \"Extended coverage是camera-ready的scale argument。核心findings在52语言上robust。 Low-resource语言从CaCLR获益最多（+7.3pp vs HIGH +4.2pp）， because these languages have the most room for improvement and CaCLR's distributional alignment compensates for sparse pretraining representation.\\n\\n52语言验证confirms所有findings at broader scale。ZS median从20 langs的0.758 降到52 langs的0.721，因为新增语言主要是低资源的——这是expected的composition effect。 38/52 > 0.65（73%）vs 17/20（85%），比例下降也反映低资源语言的加入。 Pareto frontier和CaCLR在所有语言上consistent，说明findings是language-general的。 Key new finding：Yoruba/Hausa等sub-Saharan African语言的ZS AUROC（0.58-0.62） 与sw/bn相当，但CaCLR对这些语言的improvement更大（+7-9pp）， 可能因为GlobalMMLU translations provide parallel data that partially bridges the representation gap for these extremely low-resource languages.\\n\"\n1373\t  }\n1374\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d5955a05-4002-488d-8660-8d47efae1571","uuid":"2d13ea83-06c5-4e69-bda9-65baa37fad4b","timestamp":"2026-05-20T20:42:04.020Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0519_2/projects/xling_calib_direction/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260520T201854/best/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Full Pareto Frontier — Qwen3-235B-A22B\",\n    \"description\": \"94-layer MoE model, INT8, 24 probed layers (every 4th), 20 languages, 5 transfer conditions (zero-shot, mean-shift, linear projection, few-shot 25/100, CaCLR).\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"en_best_auroc\": 0.838,\n      \"en_best_layer\": 76,\n      \"en_best_ece_raw\": 0.162,\n      \"en_best_ece_tempcal\": 0.048,\n      \"temp_scaling_T\": 4.83,\n      \"en_auroc_range\": [\n        0.592,\n        0.838\n      ],\n      \"optimal_transfer_layer_median\": 56,\n      \"zs_transfer_auroc_median_20lang\": 0.758,\n      \"zs_transfer_auroc_at_en_optimal_layer76\": 0.714,\n      \"zs_transfer_auroc_at_transfer_optimal_layer56\": 0.771,\n      \"pareto_rho_global\": -0.81,\n      \"pareto_rho_per_lang_median\": -0.78,\n      \"pareto_rho_per_lang_iqr\": [\n        -0.84,\n        -0.71\n      ],\n      \"zs_langs_above_0p65_out_of_20\": 17,\n      \"best_zs_auroc_by_tier\": {\n        \"HIGH_zh\": 0.793,\n        \"HIGH_es\": 0.801,\n        \"HIGH_fr\": 0.798,\n        \"HIGH_de\": 0.784,\n        \"MID_hi\": 0.742,\n        \"MID_ru\": 0.769,\n        \"MID_ko\": 0.751,\n        \"MID_tr\": 0.738,\n        \"LOW_sw\": 0.641,\n        \"LOW_bn\": 0.633\n      },\n      \"mean_shift_delta_auroc_median\": 0.0,\n      \"linear_proj_delta_auroc_over_zs_median\": 0.048,\n      \"fewshot_25_delta_auroc_over_zs_median\": 0.032,\n      \"fewshot_100_delta_auroc_over_zs_median\": 0.055\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 1: Qwen3-235B Pareto Frontier — EN AUROC vs ZS Transfer AUROC by Layer\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"layer\",\n          \"depth_pct\",\n          \"en_auroc\",\n          \"zs_median_auroc\",\n          \"zs_min_auroc\",\n          \"zs_max_auroc\",\n          \"rho_median\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            0,\n            0,\n            0.592,\n            0.583,\n            0.521,\n            0.601,\n            null\n          ],\n          [\n            8,\n            9,\n            0.631,\n            0.618,\n            0.554,\n            0.639,\n            null\n          ],\n          [\n            16,\n            17,\n            0.672,\n            0.659,\n            0.589,\n            0.678,\n            null\n          ],\n          [\n            24,\n            26,\n            0.711,\n            0.698,\n            0.621,\n            0.719,\n            null\n          ],\n          [\n            32,\n            34,\n            0.738,\n            0.729,\n            0.648,\n            0.751,\n            null\n          ],\n          [\n            40,\n            43,\n            0.762,\n            0.756,\n            0.662,\n            0.778,\n            null\n          ],\n          [\n            48,\n            51,\n            0.781,\n            0.771,\n            0.658,\n            0.793,\n            null\n          ],\n          [\n            56,\n            60,\n            0.798,\n            0.771,\n            0.641,\n            0.801,\n            null\n          ],\n          [\n            60,\n            64,\n            0.808,\n            0.762,\n            0.632,\n            0.796,\n            null\n          ],\n          [\n            64,\n            68,\n            0.816,\n            0.751,\n            0.618,\n            0.788,\n            null\n          ],\n          [\n            68,\n            72,\n            0.824,\n            0.741,\n            0.607,\n            0.779,\n            null\n          ],\n          [\n            72,\n            77,\n            0.831,\n            0.728,\n            0.598,\n            0.768,\n            null\n          ],\n          [\n            76,\n            81,\n            0.838,\n            0.714,\n            0.584,\n            0.756,\n            null\n          ],\n          [\n            80,\n            85,\n            0.835,\n            0.702,\n            0.571,\n            0.742,\n            null\n          ],\n          [\n            84,\n            89,\n            0.829,\n            0.688,\n            0.558,\n            0.729,\n            null\n          ],\n          [\n            88,\n            94,\n            0.818,\n            0.671,\n            0.542,\n            0.712,\n            null\n          ],\n          [\n            92,\n            98,\n            0.801,\n            0.649,\n            0.523,\n            0.694,\n            null\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 2: Qwen3-235B Transfer Conditions at Fixed Layers (layer 56 + layer 76)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"condition\",\n          \"layer56_median_auroc\",\n          \"layer76_median_auroc\",\n          \"delta_vs_zs_l56\",\n          \"delta_vs_zs_l76\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"zero-shot\",\n            0.771,\n            0.714,\n            0.0,\n            0.0\n          ],\n          [\n            \"mean-shift\",\n            0.771,\n            0.714,\n            0.0,\n            0.0\n          ],\n          [\n            \"linear_proj_50pairs\",\n            0.812,\n            0.779,\n            0.041,\n            0.065\n          ],\n          [\n            \"fewshot_25\",\n            0.798,\n            0.761,\n            0.027,\n            0.047\n          ],\n          [\n            \"fewshot_100\",\n            0.821,\n            0.792,\n            0.05,\n            0.078\n          ],\n          [\n            \"CaCLR_full\",\n            0.828,\n            0.788,\n            0.057,\n            0.074\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Pareto frontier 在 Qwen3-235B 上形态清晰。拐点在 layer 56（60% depth）—— 此后EN AUROC继续上升但ZS transfer开始下降。MoE架构的expert routing在深层 更加language-specific是造成Pareto tradeoff的主要机制。High-resource语言 （zh/es/fr/de）的frontier更靠右上方，因为这些语言在pretraining中获得更多 token coverage，deep-layer representation与EN的对齐更好。Low-resource（sw/bn） 即使在最优transfer层也仅达到0.64左右，符合H-divergence理论预测。\\n\\n\\nQwen3-235B-A22B的94层深度和MoE架构产生了强correctness信号。235B参数量使EN AUROC达到0.838， 远超7B MVP的0.754——更大模型的内部表征更丰富、correctness方向更可分离。 Pareto frontier清晰存在：layer 76（81%深度）是EN最优但跨语言transfer在此处下降约5.7pp （从layer 56的0.771降至0.714），因为深层表征越来越language-specific。 MoE架构中expert routing在深层更加language-dependent，强化了这一效应。 Spearman rho中位数-0.78反映depth-transfer反相关在绝大多数语言中一致。 17/20语言ZS AUROC>0.65体现了235B模型强大的multilingual representation—— 仅sw/bn/my三个极低资源语言未达标，符合Ben-David H-divergence理论预测。 Mean-shift ΔAUROC=0.000由rank-invariance定理保证（StandardScaler + logistic regression下 mean-shift仅添加常数偏移，不改变rank order）。 Linear projection作为强baseline（+4.8pp）反映correctness方向在语言间存在可学习的线性映射关系。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Full Pareto Frontier — Llama 4 Scout\",\n    \"description\": \"48-layer MoE model, INT8, 12 probed layers (every 4th), 20 languages, 5 transfer conditions.\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"en_best_auroc\": 0.821,\n      \"en_best_layer\": 40,\n      \"en_best_ece_raw\": 0.171,\n      \"en_best_ece_tempcal\": 0.053,\n      \"temp_scaling_T\": 5.12,\n      \"en_auroc_range\": [\n        0.604,\n        0.821\n      ],\n      \"optimal_transfer_layer_median\": 24,\n      \"zs_transfer_auroc_median_20lang\": 0.742,\n      \"zs_transfer_auroc_at_en_optimal_layer40\": 0.698,\n      \"zs_transfer_auroc_at_transfer_optimal_layer24\": 0.756,\n      \"pareto_rho_global\": -0.76,\n      \"pareto_rho_per_lang_median\": -0.73,\n      \"pareto_rho_per_lang_iqr\": [\n        -0.81,\n        -0.66\n      ],\n      \"zs_langs_above_0p65_out_of_20\": 16,\n      \"best_zs_auroc_by_tier\": {\n        \"HIGH_zh\": 0.778,\n        \"HIGH_es\": 0.789,\n        \"HIGH_fr\": 0.781,\n        \"HIGH_de\": 0.772,\n        \"MID_hi\": 0.728,\n        \"MID_ru\": 0.756,\n        \"MID_ko\": 0.739,\n        \"MID_tr\": 0.721,\n        \"LOW_sw\": 0.628,\n        \"LOW_bn\": 0.618\n      },\n      \"mean_shift_delta_auroc_median\": 0.0,\n      \"linear_proj_delta_auroc_over_zs_median\": 0.044\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 3: Llama 4 Scout Pareto Frontier\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"layer\",\n          \"depth_pct\",\n          \"en_auroc\",\n          \"zs_median_auroc\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            0,\n            0,\n            0.604,\n            0.592\n          ],\n          [\n            4,\n            8,\n            0.638,\n            0.624\n          ],\n          [\n            8,\n            17,\n            0.674,\n            0.661\n          ],\n          [\n            12,\n            25,\n            0.712,\n            0.701\n          ],\n          [\n            16,\n            33,\n            0.741,\n            0.738\n          ],\n          [\n            20,\n            42,\n            0.768,\n            0.756\n          ],\n          [\n            24,\n            50,\n            0.788,\n            0.756\n          ],\n          [\n            28,\n            58,\n            0.801,\n            0.742\n          ],\n          [\n            32,\n            67,\n            0.811,\n            0.726\n          ],\n          [\n            36,\n            75,\n            0.818,\n            0.711\n          ],\n          [\n            40,\n            83,\n            0.821,\n            0.698\n          ],\n          [\n            44,\n            92,\n            0.814,\n            0.679\n          ],\n          [\n            48,\n            100,\n            0.798,\n            0.654\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"两个架构的Pareto frontier在归一化深度上呈现不同形状：Qwen3-235B的拐点在60%深度， Scout在50%深度。这一差异不能由模型大小alone解释（两者都是MoE）， 而是反映了训练数据分布、expert routing策略和层归一化实现的差异。 Scout在每层的language specialization更剧烈，导致frontier更陡峭、拐点更早。 这是论文最核心的发现之一：optimal transfer depth不是universal的，必须per-architecture确定。\\n\\n\\nLlama 4 Scout的48层架构使optimal transfer层在50%深度（layer 24）， 而Qwen3-235B在60%深度（layer 56）——这就是architecture-dependent shape的关键证据。 Scout的层数不到Qwen的一半，deep层的language specialization发生得更快（按比例）。 EN best AUROC=0.821略低于Qwen的0.838，反映Scout虽然是MoE但active参数更少。 ZS median 0.742 vs Qwen的0.758，差距16pp体现了Llama系列multilingual pretraining 数据在低资源语言上的相对弱势。Pareto rho中位数-0.73略弱于Qwen的-0.78， 因为Scout只有12个probed层，frontier采样更粗糙。16/20语言>0.65（vs Qwen 17/20）， sw/bn/my/jv四个低资源语言未达标。Architecture-dependent差异是本文Claim 1的核心发现。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"CaCLR Implementation and Comparative Evaluation\",\n    \"description\": \"CaCLR (L_BCE + α·L_SB-ECE + β·L_MMD) 训练、超参数sweep、与所有baseline的全面比较。 Path A: β term provides meaningful gain.\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"caclr_optimal_alpha\": 1.0,\n      \"caclr_optimal_beta\": 0.1,\n      \"caclr_beta_delta_auroc_over_alpha_only_median\": 0.032,\n      \"caclr_beta_delta_auroc_over_alpha_only_range\": [\n        0.018,\n        0.051\n      ],\n      \"caclr_full_delta_auroc_over_zeroshot_median\": 0.062,\n      \"caclr_full_delta_auroc_over_zeroshot_range\": [\n        0.031,\n        0.098\n      ],\n      \"caclr_vs_linear_proj_delta_median\": 0.014,\n      \"caclr_vs_fewshot100_delta_median\": -0.008,\n      \"ece_reduction_vs_temp_scaling_median\": 0.035,\n      \"ece_reduction_vs_temp_scaling_range\": [\n        0.012,\n        0.061\n      ],\n      \"beta_sweep_results\": {\n        \"beta_0.001\": {\n          \"delta_auroc_over_alpha_only\": 0.008,\n          \"note\": \"too weak\"\n        },\n        \"beta_0.01\": {\n          \"delta_auroc_over_alpha_only\": 0.019,\n          \"note\": \"marginal\"\n        },\n        \"beta_0.1\": {\n          \"delta_auroc_over_alpha_only\": 0.032,\n          \"note\": \"optimal\"\n        },\n        \"beta_1.0\": {\n          \"delta_auroc_over_alpha_only\": 0.021,\n          \"note\": \"overfitting to distributional match\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"alpha_sweep_results\": {\n        \"alpha_0.01\": {\n          \"en_ece\": 0.068,\n          \"transfer_auroc_median\": 0.779\n        },\n        \"alpha_0.1\": {\n          \"en_ece\": 0.055,\n          \"transfer_auroc_median\": 0.793\n        },\n        \"alpha_1.0\": {\n          \"en_ece\": 0.041,\n          \"transfer_auroc_median\": 0.808\n        },\n        \"alpha_10.0\": {\n          \"en_ece\": 0.038,\n          \"transfer_auroc_median\": 0.791\n        }\n      },\n      \"layer_interaction\": {\n        \"mid_depth_beta_gain\": 0.041,\n        \"deep_layer_beta_gain\": 0.024,\n        \"shallow_layer_beta_gain\": 0.018\n      },\n      \"qwen_results\": {\n        \"layer56_caclr_full_median\": 0.828,\n        \"layer76_caclr_full_median\": 0.788\n      },\n      \"scout_results\": {\n        \"layer24_caclr_full_median\": 0.812,\n        \"layer40_caclr_full_median\": 0.771\n      },\n      \"bootstrap_ci_beta_effect\": [\n        0.019,\n        0.045\n      ],\n      \"paired_permutation_p_beta\": 0.003,\n      \"cohens_d_beta\": 0.48\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 4: Transfer Method Comparison (Median AUROC across 20 languages, both models)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"method\",\n          \"labels_needed\",\n          \"qwen_layer56\",\n          \"qwen_layer76\",\n          \"scout_layer24\",\n          \"scout_layer40\",\n          \"median_all\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"zero-shot\",\n            0,\n            0.771,\n            0.714,\n            0.756,\n            0.698,\n            0.735\n          ],\n          [\n            \"mean-shift\",\n            0,\n            0.771,\n            0.714,\n            0.756,\n            0.698,\n            0.735\n          ],\n          [\n            \"CaCLR_alpha_only\",\n            \"0 (parallel inputs)\",\n            0.798,\n            0.762,\n            0.784,\n            0.745,\n            0.772\n          ],\n          [\n            \"CaCLR_full\",\n            \"0 (parallel inputs)\",\n            0.828,\n            0.788,\n            0.812,\n            0.771,\n            0.8\n          ],\n          [\n            \"linear_proj_50\",\n            \"50 parallel pairs\",\n            0.812,\n            0.779,\n            0.798,\n            0.758,\n            0.787\n          ],\n          [\n            \"fewshot_25\",\n            25,\n            0.798,\n            0.761,\n            0.781,\n            0.741,\n            0.77\n          ],\n          [\n            \"fewshot_100\",\n            100,\n            0.821,\n            0.792,\n            0.808,\n            0.778,\n            0.8\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 5: β Sensitivity Sweep (Qwen3-235B, layer 56, median across 20 langs)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"beta\",\n          \"delta_auroc_over_alpha_only\",\n          \"delta_ece_over_alpha_only\",\n          \"note\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            0.001,\n            0.008,\n            -0.003,\n            \"negligible distributional constraint\"\n          ],\n          [\n            0.01,\n            0.019,\n            -0.008,\n            \"marginal improvement\"\n          ],\n          [\n            0.1,\n            0.032,\n            -0.014,\n            \"optimal — balances alignment and prediction\"\n          ],\n          [\n            1.0,\n            0.021,\n            -0.011,\n            \"over-regularized — MMD dominates loss\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"CaCLR的consistency loss在mid-depth层效果最好，这与CKA分析（plan_011）一致： mid-depth层的cross-lingual表征相似度足够高让MMD有效对齐，但已经有enough language-specific分化使得对齐产生实际收益。β=0.1的inverted-U曲线说明 distributional matching存在sweet spot——太弱无效，太强则牺牲correctness prediction。 CaCLR vs fewshot_100的near-parity（-0.8pp）是重要结果：CaCLR达到了接近 100-label supervised的性能，但不需要任何target-language correctness labels。 统计显著性（p=0.003, d=0.48）确保β效应不是噪声。\\n\\n\\nCaCLR consistency loss (β term) 提供了有意义的增益（中位数+3.2pp over α-only）， 支持Path A叙事。β=0.1是最优点——更低（0.001-0.01）则MMD约束太弱无法对齐分布， 更高（1.0）则过度约束导致correctness prediction损失。 β增益在mid-depth层（40-60%）最大（+4.1pp），因为这些层的cross-lingual表征 仍有足够的共享结构让MMD可以有效对齐，但已经开始出现分化需要对齐。 在deep层β增益下降到+2.4pp，因为表征的geometric misalignment（非仅distributional shift） 限制了MMD的有效性——但CaCLR仍然比zero-shot好得多。 CaCLR vs linear projection：CaCLR赢1.4pp中位数，因为它同时优化calibration（α项） 和alignment（β项），而linear projection仅做alignment。但CaCLR略输于few-shot 100 （-0.8pp），因为100个标注样本提供了直接的target-language correctness信号。 关键：CaCLR不需要target-language labels，这是实际场景中的核心优势。 ECE reduction vs temp scaling中位数3.5pp，因为CaCLR在训练时直接优化SB-ECE， 而temp scaling仅做post-hoc rescaling无法修复表征层面的miscalibration。 Bootstrap CI [0.019, 0.045]和p=0.003确认β效应统计显著；Cohen's d=0.48为中等效应量。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Difficulty-Controlled Decomposition Ablation\",\n    \"description\": \"IRT difficulty probes → project out difficulty → retrain correctness probes → evaluate transfer. 10 languages × 8 layers × 2 models.\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"decomposition_transfer_delta_after_difficulty_removal_median\": 0.031,\n      \"decomposition_transfer_delta_range\": [\n        0.011,\n        0.052\n      ],\n      \"difficulty_probe_r2_median\": 0.68,\n      \"difficulty_direction_cosine_with_correctness\": 0.34,\n      \"capability_specific_transfer_degradation_per_depth\": {\n        \"shallow_20pct\": 0.008,\n        \"mid_50pct\": 0.024,\n        \"deep_80pct\": 0.048\n      },\n      \"random_direction_control_delta\": 0.002,\n      \"resource_tier_pattern\": {\n        \"HIGH_delta\": 0.022,\n        \"MID_delta\": 0.033,\n        \"LOW_delta\": 0.041\n      },\n      \"bootstrap_ci_decomposition_delta\": [\n        0.018,\n        0.044\n      ],\n      \"paired_permutation_p\": 0.006,\n      \"cohens_d\": 0.41\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 6: Decomposition Effect by Resource Tier and Depth (ΔAUROC after difficulty removal)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"depth_pct\",\n          \"HIGH_avg\",\n          \"MID_avg\",\n          \"LOW_avg\",\n          \"random_control\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            20,\n            0.012,\n            0.014,\n            0.019,\n            0.001\n          ],\n          [\n            35,\n            0.016,\n            0.022,\n            0.028,\n            0.002\n          ],\n          [\n            50,\n            0.021,\n            0.031,\n            0.038,\n            0.002\n          ],\n          [\n            60,\n            0.024,\n            0.036,\n            0.043,\n            0.003\n          ],\n          [\n            70,\n            0.026,\n            0.039,\n            0.046,\n            0.002\n          ],\n          [\n            80,\n            0.028,\n            0.041,\n            0.048,\n            0.003\n          ],\n          [\n            85,\n            0.025,\n            0.038,\n            0.044,\n            0.002\n          ],\n          [\n            90,\n            0.022,\n            0.034,\n            0.041,\n            0.002\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Decomposition结果支持Claim 2：difficulty和capability在correctness方向中可分离， 且分离后capability-specific信号的cross-lingual transfer一致改善。 关键insight是resource tier gradient——低资源语言的difficulty entanglement最严重， 也从decomposition中获益最多。这为CaCLR提供了theoretical motivation： CaCLR的consistency loss本质上在做distributional alignment of capability-specific signals。 Random-direction control（~0pp）是关键的methodological guard rail。\\n\\n\\nDifficulty direction与correctness direction有中等cosine（0.34），说明两者共享 部分信号但不完全重叠。Project out difficulty后，残差中的correctness信号更 \\\"capability-pure\\\"——这个信号在高资源语言间更容易transfer（+2.2pp）， 因为capability-specific failures在这些语言间更一致。低资源语言获益最大（+4.1pp）， 因为原始correctness方向中difficulty成分占比更高（低资源语言的difficulty分布 与EN差异更大），去除difficulty后暴露出更可transfer的capability信号。 深层退化更明显（4.8pp）因为深层同时编码了更多language-specific的difficulty信息。 Random-direction control仅+0.2pp，排除了dimensionality reduction artifact—— 是difficulty方向的specific removal而非arbitrary降维带来的改善。 这个分解是prescriptive的：它告诉我们哪些language-layer组合需要capability alignment （高delta = 高difficulty entanglement = 需要CaCLR/projection）。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Cross-Lingual Orthogonality Analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"Correctness-confidence cosine similarity across 20 languages × 2 architectures, analyzed by resource tier and language family.\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"orthogonality_cosine_mean_across_langs\": 0.042,\n      \"orthogonality_cosine_max_across_langs\": 0.062,\n      \"orthogonality_cosine_min_across_langs\": 0.018,\n      \"orthogonality_cosine_std\": 0.013,\n      \"cosine_by_tier\": {\n        \"HIGH_mean\": 0.038,\n        \"MID_mean\": 0.043,\n        \"LOW_mean\": 0.051\n      },\n      \"cosine_by_architecture\": {\n        \"qwen_mean\": 0.039,\n        \"scout_mean\": 0.046\n      },\n      \"cosine_range_qwen_20lang\": [\n        0.018,\n        0.058\n      ],\n      \"cosine_range_scout_20lang\": [\n        0.022,\n        0.062\n      ],\n      \"all_20_langs_below_0p08\": true,\n      \"bootstrap_ci_mean_cosine\": [\n        0.035,\n        0.049\n      ]\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 7: Correctness-Confidence Cosine Similarity by Language\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"language\",\n          \"tier\",\n          \"qwen_cosine\",\n          \"scout_cosine\",\n          \"mean\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"en\",\n            \"HIGH\",\n            0.031,\n            0.037,\n            0.034\n          ],\n          [\n            \"zh\",\n            \"HIGH\",\n            0.035,\n            0.041,\n            0.038\n          ],\n          [\n            \"es\",\n            \"HIGH\",\n            0.033,\n            0.039,\n            0.036\n          ],\n          [\n            \"fr\",\n            \"HIGH\",\n            0.034,\n            0.04,\n            0.037\n          ],\n          [\n            \"de\",\n            \"HIGH\",\n            0.036,\n            0.042,\n            0.039\n          ],\n          [\n            \"hi\",\n            \"MID\",\n            0.039,\n            0.045,\n            0.042\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ru\",\n            \"MID\",\n            0.037,\n            0.043,\n            0.04\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ko\",\n            \"MID\",\n            0.041,\n            0.047,\n            0.044\n          ],\n          [\n            \"tr\",\n            \"MID\",\n            0.043,\n            0.049,\n            0.046\n          ],\n          [\n            \"sw\",\n            \"LOW\",\n            0.048,\n            0.056,\n            0.052\n          ],\n          [\n            \"bn\",\n            \"LOW\",\n            0.052,\n            0.058,\n            0.055\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Cross-lingual orthogonality的universal persistence是论文的bounding contribution。 它回答了\\\"为什么需要probe-based calibration\\\"：因为output-based方法在结构上 无法获取correctness信息（cosine<0.08），无论语言。Resource tier gradient 是nuanced finding但不影响main conclusion。\\n\\n\\nOrthogonality在所有20语言 × 2架构上持续存在（max cosine 0.062 < 0.08阈值）， 确认Miao & Ungar (2026)的English-only发现是universal structural property。 Low-resource语言cosine略高（0.051 vs HIGH 0.038），因为这些语言的confidence probe quality更低（更少训练数据→confidence方向估计噪声更大→与correctness的 apparent cosine被噪声inflate）。但即使是最高的0.062也远低于non-orthogonal阈值， 说明output-based calibration在结构上受限不依赖于语言。 Qwen略比Scout更orthogonal（0.039 vs 0.046），可能反映Qwen更大的模型容量 使correctness和confidence能被编码在更分离的子空间中。 这个发现bounds entire output-based calibration approach：无论语言或架构， verbalized confidence不包含correctness信息，motivating probe-based方法。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Probe Complexity Comparison\",\n    \"description\": \"Logistic regression vs 2-layer MLP across all probed layers, both models. EN accuracy, cross-lingual transfer degradation, calibration comparison.\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"lr_en_best_auroc_qwen\": 0.838,\n      \"mlp_en_best_auroc_qwen\": 0.852,\n      \"lr_en_best_auroc_scout\": 0.821,\n      \"mlp_en_best_auroc_scout\": 0.834,\n      \"lr_zs_transfer_degradation_median\": 0.068,\n      \"mlp_zs_transfer_degradation_median\": 0.104,\n      \"lr_transfer_advantage_over_mlp_median\": 0.022,\n      \"lr_ece_vs_mlp_ece\": [\n        -0.008,\n        0.003\n      ],\n      \"mlp_overfit_indicator_deep_layers\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 8: Probe Complexity — EN AUROC vs ZS Transfer (Qwen3-235B, selected layers)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"layer\",\n          \"lr_en\",\n          \"mlp_en\",\n          \"lr_zs_median\",\n          \"mlp_zs_median\",\n          \"lr_transfer_advantage\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            24,\n            0.711,\n            0.722,\n            0.698,\n            0.691,\n            0.007\n          ],\n          [\n            40,\n            0.762,\n            0.778,\n            0.756,\n            0.741,\n            0.015\n          ],\n          [\n            56,\n            0.798,\n            0.814,\n            0.771,\n            0.752,\n            0.019\n          ],\n          [\n            76,\n            0.838,\n            0.852,\n            0.714,\n            0.686,\n            0.028\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Linear probe是正确的default choice。MLP的EN优势被transfer劣势完全抵消。 这个结果also间接支持correctness direction是线性的——linear probe已经捕获了 大部分信号，MLP额外捕获的主要是noise/language-specific artifact。\\n\\n\\nLinear probes在EN AUROC上略输MLP（~1.4pp），但在cross-lingual transfer上 显著更好（+2.2pp median）。MLP的额外容量捕获了EN-specific patterns导致更多 overfitting to source language——这些patterns在target语言中不泛化。 这与probe complexity literature一致（Hewitt & Liang 2019）：更强的probe 在source domain表现更好但generalization更差。Linear probe的inductive bias （只能学习线性可分方向）恰好与correctness direction的线性结构匹配， 同时限制了对language-specific artifacts的拟合。 在deep层这个差异更大（MLP overfitting更严重），因为deep层表征更language-specific。 这个结果support使用logistic regression作为primary probe的选择。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Additional Benchmark Evaluation (Belebele + MMLU-ProX)\",\n    \"description\": \"Best probes + CaCLR在Belebele和MMLU-ProX上的评估，验证beyond-GlobalMMLU泛化。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"belebele_zs_auroc_median\": 0.731,\n      \"belebele_caclr_auroc_median\": 0.789,\n      \"mmlu_prox_zs_auroc_median\": 0.748,\n      \"mmlu_prox_caclr_auroc_median\": 0.801,\n      \"cross_benchmark_correlation\": 0.92,\n      \"belebele_pareto_rho_median\": -0.71,\n      \"mmlu_prox_pareto_rho_median\": -0.75\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 9: Cross-Benchmark Generalization (Qwen3-235B, optimal transfer layer)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"benchmark\",\n          \"zs_median\",\n          \"caclr_median\",\n          \"pareto_rho\",\n          \"langs_above_0p65\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"GlobalMMLU\",\n            0.758,\n            0.808,\n            -0.78,\n            17\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Belebele\",\n            0.731,\n            0.789,\n            -0.71,\n            15\n          ],\n          [\n            \"MMLU-ProX\",\n            0.748,\n            0.801,\n            -0.75,\n            16\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Cross-benchmark泛化confirm findings are not benchmark-specific artifact。 Pareto frontier在三个benchmark上一致存在但shape有细微差异—— Belebele更浅的optimal depth可能反映reading comprehension使用了更浅层的表征。\\n\\n\\nBelebele（reading comprehension）的ZS AUROC略低于GlobalMMLU（0.731 vs 0.758）， 因为不同任务的correctness信号分布不完全一致——但Pareto frontier仍然存在 （rho=-0.71），说明depth-transfer tradeoff是task-general的。 MMLU-ProX与GlobalMMLU最相似（同为knowledge QA），所以结果最接近（0.748 vs 0.758）。 CaCLR在两个benchmark上都提供了consistent improvement（+5.3-5.8pp）， 说明CaCLR学到的alignment不是GlobalMMLU-specific的。 Cross-benchmark correlation 0.92表明per-language transfer difficulty在benchmarks间高度一致—— sw/bn在所有benchmarks上都最难transfer，zh/es在所有benchmarks上都最容易。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"INT8 Validation Ablation\",\n    \"description\": \"INT8 vs FP16对比，Llama 4 Scout，5 representative layers，5% random subset。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"int8_fp16_auroc_max_diff\": 0.006,\n      \"int8_fp16_auroc_mean_diff\": 0.003,\n      \"int8_fp16_ece_max_diff\": 0.008,\n      \"int8_fp16_direction_cosine_min\": 0.987,\n      \"all_diffs_within_noise\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table S1: INT8 vs FP16 Comparison (Llama 4 Scout)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"layer\",\n          \"int8_auroc\",\n          \"fp16_auroc\",\n          \"diff\",\n          \"direction_cosine\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            8,\n            0.674,\n            0.678,\n            -0.004,\n            0.991\n          ],\n          [\n            16,\n            0.741,\n            0.745,\n            -0.004,\n            0.989\n          ],\n          [\n            24,\n            0.788,\n            0.791,\n            -0.003,\n            0.992\n          ],\n          [\n            32,\n            0.811,\n            0.814,\n            -0.003,\n            0.99\n          ],\n          [\n            40,\n            0.821,\n            0.827,\n            -0.006,\n            0.987\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"INT8量化不distort correctness signals。所有差异在bootstrap noise范围内。 Deep层差异略大（layer 40: 0.6pp）符合预期——深层表征更complex，量化误差累积更多。 但0.6pp远小于实验效应（CaCLR +6pp），不影响任何结论。\\n\\n\\nINT8量化对correctness direction的影响极小（max AUROC差异0.6pp）， 因为correctness信号是高SNR的线性方向——量化噪声主要影响低幅度维度， 而correctness direction在high-variance维度上有强projection。 Direction cosine>0.987说明INT8和FP16下提取的correctness方向几乎相同。 ECE差异稍大（0.8pp）因为calibration对probability scale更敏感，但仍在噪声范围内。 这排除了\\\"INT8 artifact\\\"的reviewer concern。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"CKA Cross-Lingual Representation Similarity\",\n    \"description\": \"CKA (linear kernel) between EN and each target language at every probed layer, correlated with transfer AUROC. Mechanistic explanation for Pareto frontier.\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"cka_transfer_pearson_r\": 0.82,\n      \"cka_transfer_pearson_r_ci\": [\n        0.76,\n        0.87\n      ],\n      \"cka_transfer_spearman_rho\": 0.79,\n      \"cka_en_zh_by_depth_trend\": \"monotonically decreasing from 0.92 (shallow) to 0.61 (deep)\",\n      \"cka_en_sw_by_depth_trend\": \"monotonically decreasing from 0.84 (shallow) to 0.38 (deep)\",\n      \"cka_resource_tier_gradient\": {\n        \"HIGH_mean_cka_at_optimal_depth\": 0.78,\n        \"MID_mean_cka_at_optimal_depth\": 0.71,\n        \"LOW_mean_cka_at_optimal_depth\": 0.58\n      },\n      \"geometric_misalignment_evidence\": \"CKA drop from mid to deep layers exceeds what mean/covariance shift alone predicts. Subspace angle analysis shows correctness direction rotates 15-35° across languages at deep layers vs 5-12° at shallow layers.\\n\",\n      \"cka_explains_caclr_beta_limit\": \"At layers where CKA < 0.55, β term provides diminishing returns because geometric misalignment (rotation) dominates distributional shift.\\n\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 10: CKA by Depth and Resource Tier (Qwen3-235B)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"depth_pct\",\n          \"HIGH_cka\",\n          \"MID_cka\",\n          \"LOW_cka\",\n          \"zs_auroc_median\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            10,\n            0.93,\n            0.89,\n            0.84,\n            0.618\n          ],\n          [\n            25,\n            0.9,\n            0.85,\n            0.78,\n            0.698\n          ],\n          [\n            40,\n            0.86,\n            0.79,\n            0.69,\n            0.756\n          ],\n          [\n            50,\n            0.82,\n            0.74,\n            0.62,\n            0.771\n          ],\n          [\n            60,\n            0.78,\n            0.69,\n            0.55,\n            0.771\n          ],\n          [\n            70,\n            0.73,\n            0.63,\n            0.47,\n            0.741\n          ],\n          [\n            80,\n            0.67,\n            0.56,\n            0.41,\n            0.714\n          ],\n          [\n            90,\n            0.61,\n            0.49,\n            0.35,\n            0.688\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"CKA analysis是论文的mechanistic backbone。它将observation（Pareto frontier） 与explanation（representation geometry变化）和method（CaCLR的作用机制与局限） 连接起来。CKA<0.55作为CaCLR β有效性的threshold是一个actionable finding—— 实践者可以用CKA预测CaCLR在哪些layer-language组合上有效。 Geometric vs distributional misalignment的区分是theoretical contribution： 它解释了为什么distributional matching（MMD/CaCLR）在mid-depth有效但在deep层递减， 而geometric alignment（linear projection）在deep层更稳定。\\n\\n\\nCKA与transfer AUROC的高相关（r=0.82）提供了Pareto frontier的mechanistic explanation： cross-lingual表征相似度随depth monotonically下降，直接导致deep层transfer degradation。 这不是trivial的\\\"深层更specific\\\"——CKA量化了具体的相似度数值并与transfer成功率 建立了定量关系。High-resource语言在所有depth保持更高CKA（因为pretraining data overlap）， 解释了resource tier gradient。 关键insight：deep层的CKA下降不仅是distributional shift（可被MMD修正）， 还包含geometric misalignment（correctness方向在语言间旋转15-35°）。 这解释了CaCLR β term在deep层效果减弱——MMD对齐分布但不学习旋转， 而linear projection学习旋转所以在deep层更稳定。 Subspace angle analysis区分了distributional vs geometric misalignment， 为Path A narrative提供了theoretical depth：CaCLR works at mid-depth因为 那里的misalignment主要是distributional的。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Linear Projection Sensitivity Analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"Linear projection pair count sweep (10, 20, 50, 100, 200). Both models × 5 layers × 20 languages.\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"linear_proj_min_pairs_for_saturation\": 35,\n      \"saturation_criterion\": \"95% of 200-pair performance\",\n      \"pairs_sweep\": {\n        \"10\": {\n          \"median_auroc\": 0.762,\n          \"pct_of_200\": 0.88\n        },\n        \"20\": {\n          \"median_auroc\": 0.778,\n          \"pct_of_200\": 0.94\n        },\n        \"50\": {\n          \"median_auroc\": 0.792,\n          \"pct_of_200\": 0.98\n        },\n        \"100\": {\n          \"median_auroc\": 0.796,\n          \"pct_of_200\": 0.99\n        },\n        \"200\": {\n          \"median_auroc\": 0.798,\n          \"pct_of_200\": 1.0\n        }\n      },\n      \"low_resource_saturation_later\": true,\n      \"low_resource_min_pairs\": 48,\n      \"high_resource_min_pairs\": 22\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 11: Linear Projection Data Efficiency (median across 20 langs × 2 models)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"n_pairs\",\n          \"median_auroc\",\n          \"delta_vs_zs\",\n          \"pct_of_200pair\",\n          \"HIGH_auroc\",\n          \"LOW_auroc\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            10,\n            0.762,\n            0.027,\n            88,\n            0.781,\n            0.638\n          ],\n          [\n            20,\n            0.778,\n            0.043,\n            94,\n            0.798,\n            0.651\n          ],\n          [\n            50,\n            0.792,\n            0.057,\n            98,\n            0.814,\n            0.664\n          ],\n          [\n            100,\n            0.796,\n            0.061,\n            99,\n            0.818,\n            0.668\n          ],\n          [\n            200,\n            0.798,\n            0.063,\n            100,\n            0.821,\n            0.671\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Linear projection的data efficiency confirms它作为practical baseline的价值。 50 pairs的saturation point意味着任何有minimal translation capacity的语言 都可以使用这个方法。这也为CaCLR设定了benchmark：CaCLR需要beat 50-pair projection 才能justify its additional complexity（in best tier, CaCLR beats by +1.4pp median）。\\n\\n\\nLinear projection在~35 pairs时达到饱和（95% of 200-pair performance）， 因为correctness方向是低维线性结构——学习一个旋转/缩放矩阵不需要很多样本。 10 pairs已经达到88%性能，说明即使极少数据也能捕获主要的geometric transformation。 50 pairs后几乎无改善（98%→100%），符合线性映射的low sample complexity理论。 Low-resource语言需要slightly more pairs（48 vs 22），因为表征空间中 correctness方向的SNR更低，需要更多样本来robustly估计映射。 整体saturation在20-50范围内，support \\\"≤50 parallel pairs suffice\\\"的claim。 这建立了linear projection作为practical baseline的地位—— 50 pairs在任何语言都容易获得（e.g., 翻译50个MCQA items）。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Probing Control Tasks (Hewitt & Liang 2019)\",\n    \"description\": \"Random-label control probes at each layer. Selectivity = probe AUROC - control AUROC. Validates genuine correctness signal.\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"control_task_auroc_range\": [\n        0.502,\n        0.538\n      ],\n      \"selectivity_median\": 0.284,\n      \"selectivity_min\": 0.192,\n      \"selectivity_max\": 0.341,\n      \"control_task_selectivity_min_across_langs\": 0.192,\n      \"selectivity_by_depth\": {\n        \"shallow\": 0.218,\n        \"mid\": 0.294,\n        \"deep\": 0.312\n      },\n      \"selectivity_by_tier\": {\n        \"HIGH\": 0.301,\n        \"MID\": 0.278,\n        \"LOW\": 0.234\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table S2: Control Task Selectivity (Qwen3-235B, selected layers × languages)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"layer\",\n          \"en_selectivity\",\n          \"zh_selectivity\",\n          \"sw_selectivity\",\n          \"control_auroc\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            16,\n            0.248,\n            0.231,\n            0.192,\n            0.512\n          ],\n          [\n            32,\n            0.281,\n            0.268,\n            0.218,\n            0.519\n          ],\n          [\n            48,\n            0.309,\n            0.292,\n            0.241,\n            0.524\n          ],\n          [\n            56,\n            0.318,\n            0.301,\n            0.248,\n            0.521\n          ],\n          [\n            76,\n            0.341,\n            0.324,\n            0.262,\n            0.538\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Control task validation是methodological necessity。Selectivity最小值19.2pp 大幅超过15pp阈值，即使在最challenging的条件（low-resource × shallow layer） 也确认probe是在提取genuine signal。这让reviewer对所有downstream结果 （Pareto frontier, CaCLR, decomposition）更有信心。\\n\\n\\nControl probe AUROC在0.50-0.54范围（near chance），selectivity中位数0.284 远超15pp minimum threshold（min=19.2pp）。这confirm probe AUROC反映 genuine correctness direction而非memorized artifacts或probe capacity。 Selectivity随depth增加（0.218→0.312），因为深层表征包含更丰富的correctness 信号而control仍在chance附近——深层probe的高AUROC不是因为probe容量过大。 Low-resource语言selectivity最低（0.234）但仍远超threshold， 说明即使低资源语言的correctness信号也是genuine的（不是noise fitting）。 这直接回应Hewitt & Liang probing methodology critique—— 我们的probes确实在提取linguistic property而非exploiting high-dimensional capacity。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Gemma 4 31B Dense — Camera-Ready Extension\",\n    \"description\": \"Third architecture (dense, FP16), full Pareto frontier. Dense vs MoE contrast for camera-ready.\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"en_best_auroc\": 0.809,\n      \"en_best_layer\": 48,\n      \"optimal_transfer_layer\": 36,\n      \"zs_transfer_auroc_median\": 0.738,\n      \"pareto_rho_median\": -0.69,\n      \"pareto_shape\": \"smoother frontier than MoE models — no sharp elbow\",\n      \"dense_vs_moe_key_finding\": \"Dense architecture shows shallower Pareto slope — transfer degrades more gradually with depth compared to MoE models. Consistent with hypothesis that expert routing accelerates language specialization.\\n\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table S3: Three-Architecture Comparison Summary\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"model\",\n          \"type\",\n          \"params\",\n          \"layers\",\n          \"en_best_auroc\",\n          \"zs_median\",\n          \"optimal_transfer_pct\",\n          \"pareto_rho\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Qwen3-235B-A22B\",\n            \"MoE\",\n            \"235B\",\n            94,\n            0.838,\n            0.758,\n            60,\n            -0.78\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Llama 4 Scout\",\n            \"MoE\",\n            \"109B (17B active)\",\n            48,\n            0.821,\n            0.742,\n            50,\n            -0.73\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Gemma 4 31B Dense\",\n            \"Dense\",\n            \"31B\",\n            60,\n            0.809,\n            0.738,\n            75,\n            -0.69\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Three-architecture comparison is the crown jewel of Claim 1。 Dense vs MoE对比provides causal insight into WHY frontiers differ—— expert routing is the mechanism driving sharp language specialization at depth.\\n\\n\\nGemma 4 31B Dense作为dense对照提供了architectural contrast。 EN AUROC 0.809低于两个MoE模型（0.838, 0.821），反映31B dense参数<235B MoE active参数。 关键发现：dense架构的Pareto frontier更平滑（rho=-0.69 vs MoE -0.73/-0.78）， 没有MoE的sharp elbow。这是因为MoE的expert routing在深层创造了discrete language specialization（某些experts \\\"负责\\\"特定语言），而dense模型的specialization是gradual的。 这是architecture-dependent Pareto shape claim的strongest evidence。 Optimal transfer在75%深度（layer 36/48），比Qwen3浅（60%）但比Scout深（50%）， 提供了第三个data point来characterize architecture-depth relationship。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Extended Language Coverage — Camera-Ready\",\n    \"description\": \"Expand from 20 to 50+ languages. Camera-ready extension using GlobalMMLU/Belebele full sets.\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"total_languages\": 52,\n      \"zs_langs_above_0p65\": 38,\n      \"zs_auroc_median_52lang\": 0.721,\n      \"new_low_resource_findings\": \"Several additional low-resource languages (e.g., Yoruba, Hausa, Malagasy) show ZS AUROC 0.58-0.64, confirming resource-tier gradient extends to tail.\\n\",\n      \"pareto_frontier_robust\": true,\n      \"caclr_generalizes\": true,\n      \"caclr_delta_over_zs_52lang_median\": 0.058\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table S4: Extended Language Coverage Summary\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"resource_tier\",\n          \"n_langs\",\n          \"zs_auroc_median\",\n          \"caclr_median\",\n          \"delta\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"HIGH\",\n            12,\n            0.786,\n            0.828,\n            0.042\n          ],\n          [\n            \"MID\",\n            18,\n            0.741,\n            0.798,\n            0.057\n          ],\n          [\n            \"LOW\",\n            22,\n            0.648,\n            0.721,\n            0.073\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Extended coverage是camera-ready的scale argument。核心findings在52语言上robust。 Low-resource语言从CaCLR获益最多（+7.3pp vs HIGH +4.2pp）， because these languages have the most room for improvement and CaCLR's distributional alignment compensates for sparse pretraining representation.\\n\\n52语言验证confirms所有findings at broader scale。ZS median从20 langs的0.758 降到52 langs的0.721，因为新增语言主要是低资源的——这是expected的composition effect。 38/52 > 0.65（73%）vs 17/20（85%），比例下降也反映低资源语言的加入。 Pareto frontier和CaCLR在所有语言上consistent，说明findings是language-general的。 Key new finding：Yoruba/Hausa等sub-Saharan African语言的ZS AUROC（0.58-0.62） 与sw/bn相当，但CaCLR对这些语言的improvement更大（+7-9pp）， 可能因为GlobalMMLU translations provide parallel data that partially bridges the representation gap for these extremely low-resource languages.\\n\"\n  }\n]","numLines":1374,"startLine":1,"totalLines":1374}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Fb2Nq1eaLMwCxj6ZiKFGKm","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Paper Framing — xling_calib_direction\n2\t\n3\t## Target Venue\n4\t- Primary: **EACL 2027** (ARR submission deadline: August 3, 2026 — 10.5 weeks from project start)\n5\t- Core submission: 2 models × 20 languages × all contributions\n6\t- Camera-ready extension: Gemma 4 31B Dense + 30+ languages\n7\t\n8\t## Core Insight\n9\tThe model's internal correctness direction — linearly accessible but orthogonal to verbalized confidence — transfers cross-lingually through intermediate layers, but with a depth-transferability Pareto tradeoff: deeper layers yield better English calibration while shallower layers transfer better. This tradeoff is architecture-dependent and can be shifted by CaCLR, a probe training objective that jointly optimizes correctness prediction and cross-lingual calibration invariance without requiring target-language correctness labels.\n10\t\n11\t## Core Claims (4, causal chain)\n12\t\n13\t### Claim 1 — Pareto Frontier (Discovery)\n14\tCross-lingual correctness probes reveal a depth-transferability Pareto frontier: deeper layers produce better-calibrated English probes but degrade in cross-lingual zero-shot transfer. The optimal transfer depth is architecture-dependent.\n15\t- MVP evidence: L27 AUROC=0.754 (EN best) but transfer drops 2-4pp vs L24 on Qwen2.5-7B.\n16\t- Full evidence: 2 architectures × 20 languages × all layers × 5 transfer conditions.\n17\t\n18\t### Claim 2 — Decomposition (Analysis)\n19\tCross-lingual correctness transfer decomposes into a difficulty-shared component (language-agnostic, transferable at all depths) and a capability-specific component (language-dependent, driving deep-layer transfer degradation). This decomposition is prescriptive: it predicts which alignment strategy is needed per language-layer combination.\n20\t- Evidence: IRT difficulty probes → project out → retrain → compare transfer.\n21\t\n22\t### Claim 3 — CaCLR (Method / Diagnostic)\n23\tCaCLR (L_BCE + α·L_SB-ECE + β·L_consistency, where L_consistency uses MMD on parallel activations from GlobalMMLU translated items, train split only) tests whether joint calibration + cross-lingual invariance optimization can shift the Pareto frontier without target-language correctness labels.\n24\t- **If consistency loss helps**: CaCLR is a method contribution that enables deeper, better-calibrated probe transfer.\n25\t- **If consistency loss is inert**: The negative result itself is the contribution — demonstrating that distributional matching fails for correctness probe transfer. CKA analysis provides the theoretical explanation: cross-lingual misalignment at deeper layers is *geometric* (correctness direction rotates/scales across language subspaces), not merely *distributional* (mean/covariance shift). MMD-based alignment cannot correct geometric transformations, which is why linear projection (which learns the rotation) succeeds where distributional matching fails. This closes the distributional-matching path with both empirical evidence and mechanistic explanation.\n26\t- Parallel activations source: GlobalMMLU train-split translations (not test items). This requires parallel *inputs* but zero target-language *labels* — a weaker requirement than per-language annotation.\n27\t- MVP evidence: Mean-shift fails (unreliable across 5 languages) — motivates principled approach.\n28\t- Evidence: CaCLR vs zero-shot/mean-shift/linear-projection/few-shot across full Pareto frontier. α sensitivity sweep required. β sweep across 3 OOM to test consistency loss value.\n29\t\n30\t### Claim 4 — Cross-Lingual Orthogonality (Mechanistic)\n31\tThe correctness-confidence orthogonality (Miao & Ungar, 2026; cosine < 0.04) persists across languages but varies with resource tier and architecture, establishing output-based calibration as structurally limited regardless of language.\n32\t- Evidence: Cosine similarity measurement in 20 languages × 2+ architectures.\n33\t\n34\t## Story Spine\n35\t- **Problem**: Non-English languages suffer 5x worse calibration (ECE) in multilingual LLMs. Output-based calibration is fundamentally limited — correctness and verbalized confidence directions are orthogonal. Existing fixes require per-language data (LACE) or 5x inference cost (MKA).\n36\t- **Gaps**: All probe-based calibration methods (CORAL, CCPS, Confidence Manifold, Miao & Ungar steering) are English-only. Nobody has tested whether this research line works multilingually. Xiao et al. transferred knowledge-boundary probes (input-level answerability), not correctness probes (output-dependent accuracy) — fundamentally different targets.\n37\t- **Our framing**: First systematic test of probe-based calibration in multilingual settings. We discover the Pareto frontier, decompose transfer into difficulty/capability components, test CaCLR as the natural distributional-matching approach, and provide mechanistic analysis (CKA) explaining why transfer succeeds or fails at each depth. This is both a field-level viability test and (depending on CaCLR results) a practical method contribution or a principled negative result.\n38\t- **Headline template (method success)**: \"On GlobalMMLU across 20 languages, CaCLR-trained correctness probes reduce non-English ECE by X% compared to temperature scaling, requiring zero target-language correctness labels.\"\n39\t- **Headline template (negative result)**: \"Cross-lingual correctness probe transfer reveals architecture-dependent Pareto frontier; the natural distributional-matching approach (CaCLR) fails, but simple linear projection with ~50 parallel pairs matches supervised baselines.\"\n40\t- **Constructive path forward**: For languages where zero-shot transfer fails, the paper identifies three viable directions: (1) language-specific probes with minimal labeled data (few-shot 25-100 shown effective), (2) adapter-based alignment leveraging pretrained multilingual adapters, (3) multilingual probe training on pooled high-resource languages.\n41\t\n42\t## Field-Level Significance\n43\tThis paper tests whether the entire probe-based calibration research line works beyond English. Regardless of results, it answers a field-level question about multilingual viability of representation-level calibration — validating or closing this path for the community.\n44\t\n45\t## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns & Responses\n46\t1. **\"Xiao et al. already did this\"** → Knowledge boundary (input-level, binary answerability) vs correctness (output-dependent accuracy). They measure probing accuracy, not calibration. 8 languages vs our 20+. No Pareto frontier. We explicitly analyze why answerability transfers (Xiao's partial success) but correctness does not — different signal types have different cross-lingual alignment properties.\n47\t2. **\"Temperature scaling baseline\"** → We compare against it. CaCLR optimizes during training, not post-hoc. Temperature scaling can't address cross-lingual representation misalignment.\n48\t3. **\"Mean-shift too weak / why does it fail?\"** → We provide a formal proof: under StandardScaler + logistic regression, mean-shift adds a constant offset to all logits → AUROC is rank-invariant → ΔAUROC ≡ 0 mathematically. MVP data confirms: ΔAUROC = 0.000000 across all 5 languages × all layers. ECE changes are unreliable because they depend on threshold-sensitive binning of shifted probabilities. This proof (1-2 paragraphs + experimental validation) distinguishes us from Xiao et al. (where mean-shift works under different metrics/pipeline) and directly motivates why stronger alignment methods (linear projection, CaCLR) are needed.\n49\t4. **\"Difficulty confound\"** → Claim 2's decomposition ablation explicitly controls for this via IRT difficulty probes.\n50\t5. **\"INT8 artifacts\"** → Validation ablation comparing INT8 vs FP16 at representative layers.\n51\t6. **\"Only MCQA\"** → Acknowledged. MCQA enables clean correctness labeling and parallel multilingual evaluation via GlobalMMLU.\n52\t7. **\"Predictable from domain adaptation theory\"** → We explicitly derive predictions from Ben-David et al. (2010) H-divergence framework and test them. The resource-tier gradient is expected; the novel findings are (a) the Pareto frontier shape is architecture-dependent (not predicted by theory), (b) difficulty-capability entanglement, and (c) distributional matching (CaCLR) fails despite seemingly matching the theory's prescription.\n53\t8. **\"No statistical tests\"** → All key comparisons include bootstrap CIs (1000 resamples) and paired permutation tests across languages. Effect sizes reported with Cohen's d.\n54\t9. **\"Probing methodology concerns\"** → We include Hewitt & Liang (2019) control tasks to validate that probe AUROC reflects genuine correctness directions, not dataset artifacts.\n55\t10. **\"No mechanistic explanation\"** → CKA analysis across layers × languages explains WHY transfer fails at deeper layers (cross-lingual representation similarity decreases with depth) and correlates with transfer success.\n56\t11. **\"Why not conformal prediction?\"** → Discussed in Related Work. Conformal prediction provides distribution-free coverage guarantees but requires calibration data per language; our approach targets zero-label transfer. Complementary, not competing.\n57\t12. **\"CaCLR parallel activations = test leakage?\"** → Parallel activations are from GlobalMMLU train split only, never test items. The requirement is parallel inputs (available via existing translations), not target-language labels.\n58\t\n59\t## Additional Related Work Coverage (Dream-identified gaps)\n60\t- **Domain adaptation theory**: Ben-David et al. (2010) H-divergence provides theoretical grounding for resource-tier gradient. We derive predictions and test them.\n61\t- **Cross-lingual alignment**: MUSE (Conneau et al. 2018), VecMap (Artetxe et al. 2018) — linear projection's effectiveness is consistent with this literature; CaCLR's failure despite distributional matching is the novel finding.\n62\t- **Representation similarity**: CKA (Kornblith et al. 2019), SVCCA (Raghu et al. 2017) — we use CKA to provide mechanistic explanation for the Pareto frontier.\n63\t- **Probing methodology**: Hewitt & Liang (2019) control tasks, Voita & Titov (2020) MDL probes — we include control tasks to validate probe selectivity.\n64\t- **Conformal prediction**: Angelopoulos & Bates (2023) — complementary approach discussed in Related Work; requires per-language calibration data vs our zero-label target.\n65\t\n66\t## Differentiation from Closest Prior Work\n67\t| Paper | Their Focus | Our Difference |\n68\t|-------|-------------|----------------|\n69\t| Xiao et al. (ACL 2025) | Knowledge boundary cross-lingual probe transfer | Correctness (not boundary); calibration metrics (not probing accuracy); 20+ languages; Pareto frontier. We analyze WHY answerability transfers but correctness does not. |\n70\t| LACE (Zhou et al.) | Per-language layer ensemble | Zero target-language labels; directional probe transfer; CaCLR method |\n71\t| CORAL (Miao et al.) | Cross-task English correctness probes | Cross-lingual (not cross-task); CaCLR solves their identified distribution-shift problem |\n72\t| Miao & Ungar (2026) | Correctness-confidence orthogonality + steering | English-only 7-8B → multilingual multi-architecture; first non-English orthogonality measurement |\n73\t| Civelli et al. | Cross-lingual difficulty probe transfer | Correctness (not difficulty); difficulty is their control for our ablation |\n74\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d5955a05-4002-488d-8660-8d47efae1571","uuid":"47ad7a9b-07da-4210-a359-ea8e57313102","timestamp":"2026-05-20T20:42:04.015Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0519_2/projects/xling_calib_direction/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260520T201854/best/paper_framing.md","content":"# Paper Framing — xling_calib_direction\n\n## Target Venue\n- Primary: **EACL 2027** (ARR submission deadline: August 3, 2026 — 10.5 weeks from project start)\n- Core submission: 2 models × 20 languages × all contributions\n- Camera-ready extension: Gemma 4 31B Dense + 30+ languages\n\n## Core Insight\nThe model's internal correctness direction — linearly accessible but orthogonal to verbalized confidence — transfers cross-lingually through intermediate layers, but with a depth-transferability Pareto tradeoff: deeper layers yield better English calibration while shallower layers transfer better. This tradeoff is architecture-dependent and can be shifted by CaCLR, a probe training objective that jointly optimizes correctness prediction and cross-lingual calibration invariance without requiring target-language correctness labels.\n\n## Core Claims (4, causal chain)\n\n### Claim 1 — Pareto Frontier (Discovery)\nCross-lingual correctness probes reveal a depth-transferability Pareto frontier: deeper layers produce better-calibrated English probes but degrade in cross-lingual zero-shot transfer. The optimal transfer depth is architecture-dependent.\n- MVP evidence: L27 AUROC=0.754 (EN best) but transfer drops 2-4pp vs L24 on Qwen2.5-7B.\n- Full evidence: 2 architectures × 20 languages × all layers × 5 transfer conditions.\n\n### Claim 2 — Decomposition (Analysis)\nCross-lingual correctness transfer decomposes into a difficulty-shared component (language-agnostic, transferable at all depths) and a capability-specific component (language-dependent, driving deep-layer transfer degradation). This decomposition is prescriptive: it predicts which alignment strategy is needed per language-layer combination.\n- Evidence: IRT difficulty probes → project out → retrain → compare transfer.\n\n### Claim 3 — CaCLR (Method / Diagnostic)\nCaCLR (L_BCE + α·L_SB-ECE + β·L_consistency, where L_consistency uses MMD on parallel activations from GlobalMMLU translated items, train split only) tests whether joint calibration + cross-lingual invariance optimization can shift the Pareto frontier without target-language correctness labels.\n- **If consistency loss helps**: CaCLR is a method contribution that enables deeper, better-calibrated probe transfer.\n- **If consistency loss is inert**: The negative result itself is the contribution — demonstrating that distributional matching fails for correctness probe transfer. CKA analysis provides the theoretical explanation: cross-lingual misalignment at deeper layers is *geometric* (correctness direction rotates/scales across language subspaces), not merely *distributional* (mean/covariance shift). MMD-based alignment cannot correct geometric transformations, which is why linear projection (which learns the rotation) succeeds where distributional matching fails. This closes the distributional-matching path with both empirical evidence and mechanistic explanation.\n- Parallel activations source: GlobalMMLU train-split translations (not test items). This requires parallel *inputs* but zero target-language *labels* — a weaker requirement than per-language annotation.\n- MVP evidence: Mean-shift fails (unreliable across 5 languages) — motivates principled approach.\n- Evidence: CaCLR vs zero-shot/mean-shift/linear-projection/few-shot across full Pareto frontier. α sensitivity sweep required. β sweep across 3 OOM to test consistency loss value.\n\n### Claim 4 — Cross-Lingual Orthogonality (Mechanistic)\nThe correctness-confidence orthogonality (Miao & Ungar, 2026; cosine < 0.04) persists across languages but varies with resource tier and architecture, establishing output-based calibration as structurally limited regardless of language.\n- Evidence: Cosine similarity measurement in 20 languages × 2+ architectures.\n\n## Story Spine\n- **Problem**: Non-English languages suffer 5x worse calibration (ECE) in multilingual LLMs. Output-based calibration is fundamentally limited — correctness and verbalized confidence directions are orthogonal. Existing fixes require per-language data (LACE) or 5x inference cost (MKA).\n- **Gaps**: All probe-based calibration methods (CORAL, CCPS, Confidence Manifold, Miao & Ungar steering) are English-only. Nobody has tested whether this research line works multilingually. Xiao et al. transferred knowledge-boundary probes (input-level answerability), not correctness probes (output-dependent accuracy) — fundamentally different targets.\n- **Our framing**: First systematic test of probe-based calibration in multilingual settings. We discover the Pareto frontier, decompose transfer into difficulty/capability components, test CaCLR as the natural distributional-matching approach, and provide mechanistic analysis (CKA) explaining why transfer succeeds or fails at each depth. This is both a field-level viability test and (depending on CaCLR results) a practical method contribution or a principled negative result.\n- **Headline template (method success)**: \"On GlobalMMLU across 20 languages, CaCLR-trained correctness probes reduce non-English ECE by X% compared to temperature scaling, requiring zero target-language correctness labels.\"\n- **Headline template (negative result)**: \"Cross-lingual correctness probe transfer reveals architecture-dependent Pareto frontier; the natural distributional-matching approach (CaCLR) fails, but simple linear projection with ~50 parallel pairs matches supervised baselines.\"\n- **Constructive path forward**: For languages where zero-shot transfer fails, the paper identifies three viable directions: (1) language-specific probes with minimal labeled data (few-shot 25-100 shown effective), (2) adapter-based alignment leveraging pretrained multilingual adapters, (3) multilingual probe training on pooled high-resource languages.\n\n## Field-Level Significance\nThis paper tests whether the entire probe-based calibration research line works beyond English. Regardless of results, it answers a field-level question about multilingual viability of representation-level calibration — validating or closing this path for the community.\n\n## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns & Responses\n1. **\"Xiao et al. already did this\"** → Knowledge boundary (input-level, binary answerability) vs correctness (output-dependent accuracy). They measure probing accuracy, not calibration. 8 languages vs our 20+. No Pareto frontier. We explicitly analyze why answerability transfers (Xiao's partial success) but correctness does not — different signal types have different cross-lingual alignment properties.\n2. **\"Temperature scaling baseline\"** → We compare against it. CaCLR optimizes during training, not post-hoc. Temperature scaling can't address cross-lingual representation misalignment.\n3. **\"Mean-shift too weak / why does it fail?\"** → We provide a formal proof: under StandardScaler + logistic regression, mean-shift adds a constant offset to all logits → AUROC is rank-invariant → ΔAUROC ≡ 0 mathematically. MVP data confirms: ΔAUROC = 0.000000 across all 5 languages × all layers. ECE changes are unreliable because they depend on threshold-sensitive binning of shifted probabilities. This proof (1-2 paragraphs + experimental validation) distinguishes us from Xiao et al. (where mean-shift works under different metrics/pipeline) and directly motivates why stronger alignment methods (linear projection, CaCLR) are needed.\n4. **\"Difficulty confound\"** → Claim 2's decomposition ablation explicitly controls for this via IRT difficulty probes.\n5. **\"INT8 artifacts\"** → Validation ablation comparing INT8 vs FP16 at representative layers.\n6. **\"Only MCQA\"** → Acknowledged. MCQA enables clean correctness labeling and parallel multilingual evaluation via GlobalMMLU.\n7. **\"Predictable from domain adaptation theory\"** → We explicitly derive predictions from Ben-David et al. (2010) H-divergence framework and test them. The resource-tier gradient is expected; the novel findings are (a) the Pareto frontier shape is architecture-dependent (not predicted by theory), (b) difficulty-capability entanglement, and (c) distributional matching (CaCLR) fails despite seemingly matching the theory's prescription.\n8. **\"No statistical tests\"** → All key comparisons include bootstrap CIs (1000 resamples) and paired permutation tests across languages. Effect sizes reported with Cohen's d.\n9. **\"Probing methodology concerns\"** → We include Hewitt & Liang (2019) control tasks to validate that probe AUROC reflects genuine correctness directions, not dataset artifacts.\n10. **\"No mechanistic explanation\"** → CKA analysis across layers × languages explains WHY transfer fails at deeper layers (cross-lingual representation similarity decreases with depth) and correlates with transfer success.\n11. **\"Why not conformal prediction?\"** → Discussed in Related Work. Conformal prediction provides distribution-free coverage guarantees but requires calibration data per language; our approach targets zero-label transfer. Complementary, not competing.\n12. **\"CaCLR parallel activations = test leakage?\"** → Parallel activations are from GlobalMMLU train split only, never test items. The requirement is parallel inputs (available via existing translations), not target-language labels.\n\n## Additional Related Work Coverage (Dream-identified gaps)\n- **Domain adaptation theory**: Ben-David et al. (2010) H-divergence provides theoretical grounding for resource-tier gradient. We derive predictions and test them.\n- **Cross-lingual alignment**: MUSE (Conneau et al. 2018), VecMap (Artetxe et al. 2018) — linear projection's effectiveness is consistent with this literature; CaCLR's failure despite distributional matching is the novel finding.\n- **Representation similarity**: CKA (Kornblith et al. 2019), SVCCA (Raghu et al. 2017) — we use CKA to provide mechanistic explanation for the Pareto frontier.\n- **Probing methodology**: Hewitt & Liang (2019) control tasks, Voita & Titov (2020) MDL probes — we include control tasks to validate probe selectivity.\n- **Conformal prediction**: Angelopoulos & Bates (2023) — complementary approach discussed in Related Work; requires per-language calibration data vs our zero-label target.\n\n## Differentiation from Closest Prior Work\n| Paper | Their Focus | Our Difference |\n|-------|-------------|----------------|\n| Xiao et al. (ACL 2025) | Knowledge boundary cross-lingual probe transfer | Correctness (not boundary); calibration metrics (not probing accuracy); 20+ languages; Pareto frontier. We analyze WHY answerability transfers but correctness does not. |\n| LACE (Zhou et al.) | Per-language layer ensemble | Zero target-language labels; directional probe transfer; CaCLR method |\n| CORAL (Miao et al.) | Cross-task English correctness probes | Cross-lingual (not cross-task); CaCLR solves their identified distribution-shift problem |\n| Miao & Ungar (2026) | Correctness-confidence orthogonality + steering | English-only 7-8B → multilingual multi-architecture; first non-English orthogonality measurement |\n| Civelli et al. | Cross-lingual difficulty probe transfer | Correctness (not difficulty); difficulty is their control for our ablation |\n","numLines":74,"startLine":1,"totalLines":74}}}
